<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<usx version="3.1">
<book code="ACT" style="id">BLB-Draft</book>

<para style="h">Acts</para>

<para style="toc1">Acts</para>

<para style="rem">sourceUrl=https://literalbible.com/blb.docx fetchedAtUtc=2026-09-01T15:43:00Z status=draft id=BLB-Draft spec=USFM-USX 3.1.1 char:add=docx-italic note:f=docx-footnotes note:x=docx-heading-crossrefs</para>

<chapter number="1" style="c" sid="ACT 1"/>

<para style="s">Prologue</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 1:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 1:1–4</char></note>The first account, indeed, I made concerning all the things, O Theophilus, that Jesus began both to do and to teach, <verse eid="ACT 1:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 1:2"/>until the day <char style="add">in</char> which, having given commands through the Holy Spirit to the apostles whom He chose, He was taken up, <verse eid="ACT 1:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 1:3"/>to whom He also presented Himself alive after His suffering, with many convincing proofs, being seen by them through forty days and speaking the things concerning the kingdom of God. <verse eid="ACT 1:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 1:4"/>And being assembled together,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">eating together</char></note> He instructed them not to depart from Jerusalem, but to await the promise of the Father: <char style="wj">“That which you⁺ heard of Me; </char><verse eid="ACT 1:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 1:5"/><char style="wj">for John indeed baptized with water, but you⁺ will be baptized with the Holy Spirit not many days after these.”</char> <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">for John indeed baptized in water, but you⁺ will be baptized in the Holy Spirit not many days after these</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; cited in Acts 11:16</char></note><verse eid="ACT 1:5"/></para>

<para style="s">The AscensionMark 16:19–20</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 1:6"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Luke 24:50–53</char></note>Therefore indeed those having come together were asking Him, saying, “Lord, at this time do You restore the kingdom to Israel?” <verse eid="ACT 1:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 1:7"/>And He said to them, <char style="wj">“It is not yours⁺ to know times or seasons that the Father set by His own authority. </char><verse eid="ACT 1:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 1:8"/><char style="wj">But you⁺ will receive power at the Holy Spirit having come upon you⁺, and you⁺ will be My witnesses,</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Witnesses unto Me</char></note><char style="wj"> both in Jerusalem, and in all Judea and Samaria, and to the end of the earth.”</char> <verse eid="ACT 1:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 1:9"/>And having said these things, <char style="add">in</char> their looking on, He was lifted up, and a cloud took Him from their eyes. <verse eid="ACT 1:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 1:10"/>And as they were looking intently into heaven <char style="add">in</char> His going, then behold, two men in white apparel stood by them, <verse eid="ACT 1:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 1:11"/>who also said, “Men, Galileans, why do you⁺ stand looking<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">staring</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">gazing up</char></note> into heaven? This Jesus, having been taken up from you⁺ into heaven, will thus come in that manner you⁺ saw Him going into heaven.” <verse eid="ACT 1:11"/></para>

<para style="s">Matthias Replaces Judas</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 1:12"/>Then they returned to Jerusalem from the mount called Olivet,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Mount of Olives</char></note> which is near Jerusalem, holding a Sabbath’s journey.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">A Sabbath’s journey</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is 2,000 cubits (approximately 3,000 feet or 914.4 meters)</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 1:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 1:13"/>And when they had entered, they went up into the upper room where they were staying, both Peter and John, and James and Andrew,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Peter and James, John and Andrew</char></note> Philip and Thomas, Bartholomew and Matthew, James <char style="add">son</char> of Alphaeus and Simon the Zealot, and Judas <char style="add">son</char> of James. <verse eid="ACT 1:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 1:14"/>All these were steadfastly continuing with one accord in prayer,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and petition</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> with the women, and Mary the mother of Jesus, and with His brothers. <verse eid="ACT 1:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 1:15"/>And in these days, Peter, having risen up in the midst of the brothers,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the disciples</char></note> said (and the multitude of names at the same <char style="add">place</char> was about a hundred twenty), <verse eid="ACT 1:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 1:16"/>“Men, brothers, it was necessary for the Scripture<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">this Scripture</char></note> to have been fulfilled that the Holy Spirit spoke beforehand by the mouth of David concerning Judas, the one having become guide to those having arrested Jesus. <verse eid="ACT 1:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 1:17"/>For he was numbered among us and was allotted the share of this ministry.” <verse eid="ACT 1:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 1:18"/>(Then indeed this <char style="add">man</char> acquired a field out of the reward of unrighteousness, and having fallen headlong, he burst open in the middle, and all his intestines poured out. <verse eid="ACT 1:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 1:19"/>And it became known to all those dwelling in Jerusalem, so that that field was called in their own language Akeldama, that is, Field of Blood.) <verse eid="ACT 1:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 1:20"/>“For it has been written in the book of Psalms: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="ACT 1:20">‘May his homestead become desolate, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 1:20">and let there be no one dwelling in it,’ </para>

<para style="p" vid="ACT 1:20">and, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="ACT 1:20">‘May another take his oversight.’<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Psalm 69:25</char></note> <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Psalm 109:8</char></note><verse eid="ACT 1:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 1:21"/>Therefore it is necessary for the men having accompanied us in all the time that the Lord Jesus came in and went out among us, <verse eid="ACT 1:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 1:22"/>having begun from the baptism of John until the day in which He was taken up from us, one of these, to become a witness with us of His resurrection.” <verse eid="ACT 1:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 1:23"/>And they set two, Joseph called Barsabbas,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.23 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Barsabas</char></note> who was called upon <char style="add">as</char> Justus, and Matthias. <verse eid="ACT 1:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 1:24"/>And having prayed, they said, “You, Lord, knower of the heart of all, show which one of these two You chose <verse eid="ACT 1:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 1:25"/>to take the place of this<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to receive a share of this</char></note> ministry and apostleship, from which Judas turned aside to go to <char style="add">his</char> own place.” <verse eid="ACT 1:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 1:26"/>And they gave lots for them, and the lot fell on Matthias, and he was numbered with the eleven apostles. <verse eid="ACT 1:26"/></para>

<chapter eid="ACT 1"/>

<chapter number="2" style="c" sid="ACT 2"/>

<para style="s">The Holy Spirit at Pentecost</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 2:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Leviticus 23:15–22</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Genesis 11:1–9</char></note>And in the arriving of the day of Pentecost,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, Shavuot, the late spring feast of pilgrimage to Jerusalem; it is also known as </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Feast of Harvest</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> (see Exodus 23:16) or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Feast of Weeks</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> (see Exodus 34:22).</char></note> they were all together<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">were all with one accord</char></note> at the same <char style="add">place</char>. <verse eid="ACT 2:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 2:2"/>And suddenly a sound like a violent rushing of wind came out of heaven, and it filled the whole house where they were sitting. <verse eid="ACT 2:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 2:3"/>And there appeared to them dividing tongues as of fire, and they sat upon each one of them. <verse eid="ACT 2:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 2:4"/>And they were all filled with the Holy Spirit and began to speak in other tongues as the Spirit was giving to them to declare forth. <verse eid="ACT 2:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 2:5"/>Now there were Jews dwelling<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">staying</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; similarly in verse 14</char></note> in Jerusalem, devout men from every nation under heaven. <verse eid="ACT 2:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 2:6"/>Now this sound having happened, the multitude came together and was confounded, because each one was hearing them speaking in <char style="add">his</char> own language. <verse eid="ACT 2:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 2:7"/>And they were amazed and were marveling, saying,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to one another</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> “Behold, are not all<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> HF, NA, F35, SBL, and WH do not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">all</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> these who are speaking Galileans? <verse eid="ACT 2:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 2:8"/>And how do we each hear our own language in which we were born? <verse eid="ACT 2:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 2:9"/>Parthians and Medes and Elamites; and those inhabiting Mesopotamia, also Judea and Cappadocia, Pontus and Asia,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, the Roman Province of Asia, located in what is now western Turkey</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 2:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 2:10"/>both Phrygia and Pamphylia, Egypt and the parts of Libya that <char style="add">are</char> around Cyrene; and those visiting from Rome, <verse eid="ACT 2:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 2:11"/>both Jews and converts; Cretans and Arabs—we hear them speaking <char style="add">in</char> our own tongues the great things of God!” <verse eid="ACT 2:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 2:12"/>And all were amazed and were perplexed, saying to one another, “What does this wish to be?” <verse eid="ACT 2:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 2:13"/>But others, mocking, were saying, “They are full of new wine!” <verse eid="ACT 2:13"/></para>

<para style="s">Peter Addresses the CrowdPsalm 16:1–11</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 2:14"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Joel 2:28–32</char></note>But Peter, having stood up with the Eleven, lifted up his voice and declared forth to them: “Men of Judea and all those inhabiting Jerusalem, let this be known to you⁺, and give heed to my words. <verse eid="ACT 2:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 2:15"/>For these are not drunkards, as you⁺ suppose, for it is the third hour of the day!<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, nine in the morning</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 2:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 2:16"/>But this is that having been spoken by the prophet Joel: <verse eid="ACT 2:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 2:17"/>‘And it will come to pass in the last days, God says, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:17"><char style="add">that</char> I will pour out from My Spirit upon all flesh, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="ACT 2:17">and your⁺ sons and your⁺ daughters will prophesy, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:17">and your⁺ young men will see visions, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:17">and your⁺ old men will dream dreams. <verse eid="ACT 2:17"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 2:18"/>And even on My menservants and on My maidservants </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:18">I will pour out from My Spirit in those days, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:18">and they will prophesy. <verse eid="ACT 2:18"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 2:19"/>And I will show wonders in the heaven above </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:19">and signs on the earth below, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:19">blood and fire and vapor of smoke. <verse eid="ACT 2:19"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 2:20"/>The sun will be turned into darkness, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:20">and the moon into blood, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:20">before the coming Day of the Lord, great and glorious. <verse eid="ACT 2:20"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 2:21"/>And it will come to pass <char style="add">that</char> everyone who shall call upon the name of the Lord </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:21">will be saved.” <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.21 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Joel 2:28–32 (see also LXX)</char></note><verse eid="ACT 2:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 2:22"/>Men, Israelites, hear these words: Jesus of Nazareth, a man having been set forth by God to you⁺ by miracles and wonders and signs, which God did through Him in your⁺ midst, as you yourselves know, <verse eid="ACT 2:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 2:23"/>Him delivered up by the determinate counsel and foreknowledge of God, you⁺ put to death, having crucified by<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.23 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">having taken by</char></note> lawless hands— <verse eid="ACT 2:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 2:24"/>whom God raised up, having loosed the agony of death, inasmuch as it was not possible <char style="add">for</char> Him to be held by it. <verse eid="ACT 2:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 2:25"/>For David says about Him: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="ACT 2:25">‘I foresaw the Lord before me through all, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:25">because He is at my right hand, that I should not be shaken. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">I saw</char></note><verse eid="ACT 2:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 2:26"/>Because of this my heart was glad and my tongue rejoiced, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:26">and now also my flesh will dwell in hope, <verse eid="ACT 2:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 2:27"/>for You will not abandon my soul into Hades, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:27">nor will You give Your Holy One to see decay. <verse eid="ACT 2:27"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 2:28"/>You made known to me the paths of life; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:28">You will fill me with joy in Your presence.’<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.28 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Psalm 16:8–11 (see also LXX)</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 2:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 2:29"/>Men, brothers, it is permitted <char style="add">me</char> to speak with freedom to you⁺ concerning the patriarch David, that he both died and was buried, and his tomb is among us unto this day, <verse eid="ACT 2:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 2:30"/>being therefore a prophet and knowing that God swore to him with an oath to seat one out of the fruit of his loins upon his throne.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.30 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">one of his descendants</char></note> <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.30 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">with an oath out of the fruit of his loins, according to the flesh, to raise up Christ to sit on his throne</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; Psalm 132:11</char></note><verse eid="ACT 2:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 2:31"/>Having foreseen, he spoke concerning the resurrection of the Christ, that neither was He abandoned<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.31 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">neither was His soul abandoned</char></note> into Hades, nor did His flesh see decay. <verse eid="ACT 2:31"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 2:32"/>This Jesus God raised up, of which we all are witnesses. <verse eid="ACT 2:32"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 2:33"/>Therefore, having been exalted to the right hand of God and having received the promise of the Holy Spirit from the Father, He poured out this which you⁺ both see and hear. <verse eid="ACT 2:33"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 2:34"/>For David did not ascend into the heavens, but he himself says: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="ACT 2:34">‘The Lord said to my Lord, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:34">“Sit at My right hand <verse eid="ACT 2:34"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 2:35"/>until I place Your enemies </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 2:35"><char style="add">as</char> a footstool for Your feet.”’ <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.35 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Psalm 110:1</char></note><verse eid="ACT 2:35"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 2:36"/>Therefore let all the house of Israel know assuredly that God made Him both Lord and Christ—this Jesus whom you⁺ crucified.” <verse eid="ACT 2:36"/></para>

<para style="s">Three Thousand Believe</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 2:37"/>And having heard, they were pierced to the heart and said to Peter and the other apostles, “Men, brothers, what shall we do?” <verse eid="ACT 2:37"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 2:38"/>And Peter says to them, “Repent and be baptized, every one of you⁺, in the name of Jesus Christ for the forgiveness of your⁺ sins,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.38 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">forgiveness of sins</char></note> and you⁺ will receive the gift of the Holy Spirit. <verse eid="ACT 2:38"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="ACT 2:39"/>For the promise is to you⁺ and to your⁺ children and to all those at a distance, as many as the Lord our God shall summon.” <verse eid="ACT 2:39"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="ACT 2:40"/>And he earnestly testified many other words and was exhorting them, saying, “Be saved from this crooked generation.” <verse eid="ACT 2:40"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="ACT 2:41"/>Therefore those indeed having received<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.41 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">having gladly received</char></note> his word were baptized, and on that day about three thousand souls were added.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.41 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">about three thousand were added to the believers that day</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 2:41"/></para>

<para style="s">The Fellowship of BelieversActs 4:32–37</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="ACT 2:42"/>Now they were steadfastly continuing in the teaching of the apostles and in the fellowship, in the breaking of the bread and in the prayers. <verse eid="ACT 2:42"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="ACT 2:43"/>And fear<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.43 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">awe</char></note> was coming upon every soul, and many wonders and signs were taking place through the apostles. <verse eid="ACT 2:43"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="44" style="v" sid="ACT 2:44"/>And all those believing were in the same <char style="add">place</char> and were having all things in common. <verse eid="ACT 2:44"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="45" style="v" sid="ACT 2:45"/>And they were selling the possessions and the goods and were dividing them to all, as anyone had need. <verse eid="ACT 2:45"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="46" style="v" sid="ACT 2:46"/>And every day they were steadfastly continuing with one accord in the temple<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.46 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the temple courts</char></note> and breaking bread at each house. They were partaking of food with gladness and sincerity of heart, <verse eid="ACT 2:46"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="47" style="v" sid="ACT 2:47"/>praising God and having favor with all the people. And the Lord kept adding every day to the same<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">2.47 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to the church</char></note> those being saved. <verse eid="ACT 2:47"/></para>

<chapter eid="ACT 2"/>

<chapter number="3" style="c" sid="ACT 3"/>

<para style="s">A Lame Man Walks</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 3:1"/>Now Peter and John were going up<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">together</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> into the temple at the hour of prayer, the ninth.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, three in the afternoon</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 3:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 3:2"/>And a certain man was being carried, being lame from his mother’s womb, whom they placed every day at the temple gate called Beautiful to ask for alms from those going into the temple,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the temple courts</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verses 3 and 8</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 3:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 3:3"/>who, having seen Peter and John being about to enter into the temple, was asking to receive alms. <verse eid="ACT 3:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 3:4"/>And Peter, having looked intently upon him, with John, said, “Look toward us!” <verse eid="ACT 3:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 3:5"/>And he began to give heed to them, expecting to receive something from them. <verse eid="ACT 3:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 3:6"/>But Peter said, “Silver and gold, unto me there is none; but what I have, this I give to you: In the name of Jesus Christ of Nazareth, rise up and walk!”<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> SBL, NE, and WH </char><char style="fq" closed="false">In the name of Jesus Christ of Nazareth, walk!</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 3:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 3:7"/>And having taken him by the right hand, he raised him up, and immediately his feet and ankles were strengthened. <verse eid="ACT 3:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 3:8"/>And leaping up, he stood and began walking, and he entered into the temple with them, walking and leaping and praising God. <verse eid="ACT 3:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 3:9"/>And all the people saw him walking and praising God, <verse eid="ACT 3:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 3:10"/>and they recognized him, that he was the one sitting for alms at the Beautiful Gate of the temple. And they were filled with wonder and amazement at that having happened to him. <verse eid="ACT 3:10"/></para>

<para style="s">Peter Speaks in Solomon’s ColonnadeDeuteronomy 18:15–22</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 3:11"/>Now of him clinging to<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Now as the lame man who was healed was clinging to</char></note> Peter and John, all the people ran together to them in the colonnade called Solomon’s,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in the walkway called Solomon’s Colonnade</char></note> greatly amazed. <verse eid="ACT 3:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 3:12"/>But having seen, Peter answered to the people: “Men, Israelites, why do you⁺ wonder at this? Or why do you⁺ look intently on us as if by <char style="add">our</char> own power or godliness <char style="add">we</char> have made him to walk? <verse eid="ACT 3:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 3:13"/>The God of Abraham, and the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob, the God of our fathers, has glorified His servant<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">His child</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verse 26</char></note> Jesus, whom indeed you⁺ delivered up and denied in the presence of Pilate, that one having adjudged to release <char style="add">Him</char>. <verse eid="ACT 3:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 3:14"/>But you⁺ denied the Holy and Righteous One and requested a man, a murderer, to be granted to you⁺. <verse eid="ACT 3:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 3:15"/>And you⁺ killed the Author of life, whom God raised out from the dead, of which we are witnesses. <verse eid="ACT 3:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 3:16"/>And on the faith in His name, this <char style="add">man</char> whom you⁺ see and know, His name strengthened; and the faith that <char style="add">is</char> through Him has given to him this complete soundness before all of you⁺. <verse eid="ACT 3:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 3:17"/>And now, brothers, I know that you⁺ acted in ignorance, as your⁺ rulers also. <verse eid="ACT 3:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 3:18"/>But what God foretold through the mouth of all the prophets, <char style="add">that</char> His Christ should suffer, He thus fulfilled. <verse eid="ACT 3:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 3:19"/>Repent, therefore, and turn back, for the blotting out of your⁺ sins, <verse eid="ACT 3:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 3:20"/>so that times of refreshing may come from the presence of the Lord, and <char style="add">that</char> He may send the One having been appointed to you⁺, Christ Jesus, <verse eid="ACT 3:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 3:21"/>whom indeed it is necessary for heaven to receive until the times of restoration of all things, of which God spoke by the mouth of<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.21 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">all</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> His holy prophets from the age. <verse eid="ACT 3:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 3:22"/>Indeed Moses said, ‘The Lord your⁺ God will raise up to you⁺ a prophet like me out of your⁺ brothers. You⁺ will listen to Him in all things, as many as He might say to you⁺.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to the fathers</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Deuteronomy 18:15</char></note><verse eid="ACT 3:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 3:23"/>And it will come to pass <char style="add">that</char> every soul who might not heed that prophet will be utterly destroyed out of the people.’ <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.23 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> See Deuteronomy 18:19.</char></note><verse eid="ACT 3:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 3:24"/>And also all the prophets from Samuel, and those subsequently, as many as have spoken—they also proclaimed<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.24 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> ALT, F35, and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">foretold</char></note> these days. <verse eid="ACT 3:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 3:25"/>You⁺ are the sons of the prophets and of the covenant that God made with your⁺ fathers, saying to Abraham, ‘And in your seed all the families of the earth will be blessed.’<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">our fathers</char></note> <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Genesis 22:18</char></note><verse eid="ACT 3:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 3:26"/>God, having raised up His servant,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">3.26 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">His Servant Jesus</char></note> sent Him first to you⁺, blessing you⁺ in turning away each one from your⁺ wickednesses.” <verse eid="ACT 3:26"/></para>

<chapter eid="ACT 3"/>

<chapter number="4" style="c" sid="ACT 4"/>

<para style="s">Peter and John before the Sanhedrin</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 4:1"/>And of them speaking to the people, the priests<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> WH </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the chief priests</char></note> and the captain of the temple and the Sadducees came upon them, <verse eid="ACT 4:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 4:2"/>being distressed because of their teaching the people and proclaiming in Jesus the resurrection out from the dead. <verse eid="ACT 4:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 4:3"/>And they laid hands on them and put <char style="add">them</char> in custody until the next day, for it was already evening. <verse eid="ACT 4:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 4:4"/>But many of those having heard the word believed, and the number of the men became about five thousand. <verse eid="ACT 4:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 4:5"/>And it came to pass on the next day <char style="add">that</char> their rulers and elders and scribes were gathered together in Jerusalem, <verse eid="ACT 4:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 4:6"/>and Annas the high priest, and Caiaphas, and John, and Alexander, and as many as were of high-priestly descent. <verse eid="ACT 4:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 4:7"/>And having placed them in the midst, they began to inquire, “In what power or in what name did you⁺ do this?” <verse eid="ACT 4:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 4:8"/>Then Peter, having been filled with the Holy Spirit, said to them, “Rulers of the people and elders,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of Israel</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 4:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 4:9"/>if we are being examined this day as to a good work <char style="add">to</char> the ailing man, how<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">by whom</char></note> he has been healed, <verse eid="ACT 4:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 4:10"/>let it be known to all <char style="add">of</char> you⁺, and to all the people of Israel, that in the name of Jesus Christ of Nazareth—whom you⁺ crucified, whom God raised out from the dead—in Him this <char style="add">man</char> stands before you⁺ sound. <verse eid="ACT 4:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 4:11"/>This is </para>

<para style="q1" vid="ACT 4:11">‘the stone having been rejected by you⁺, the builders, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 4:11">which has become the head of the corner.’ <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Psalm 118:22</char></note><verse eid="ACT 4:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 4:12"/>And there is salvation in no other, for there is not another name under heaven<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> RP does not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">under heaven</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> having been given among men by which it is necessary for us to be saved.” <verse eid="ACT 4:12"/></para>

<para style="s">The Name Forbidden</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 4:13"/>Now seeing the boldness of Peter and of John, and having understood that they are unschooled and ordinary men, they were astonished. And they recognized them, that they had been with Jesus. <verse eid="ACT 4:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 4:14"/>And beholding the man having been healed standing with them, they had nothing to contradict. <verse eid="ACT 4:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 4:15"/>But having commanded them to go outside the Council,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Sanhedrin</char></note> they began to confer with one another, <verse eid="ACT 4:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 4:16"/>saying, “What shall we do to these men? For truly that a noteworthy sign has come to pass through them <char style="add">is</char> evident to all those dwelling in Jerusalem, and we are not able to deny <char style="add">it</char>. <verse eid="ACT 4:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 4:17"/>But so that it might not spread further on among the people, let us threaten<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">strictly threaten</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> them to speak no longer in this name to <char style="add">any</char> man.” <verse eid="ACT 4:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 4:18"/>And having summoned them, they commanded <char style="add">them</char> not to speak, nor to teach at all, in the name of Jesus. <verse eid="ACT 4:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 4:19"/>But Peter and John, answering, said to them, “Whether it is right before God to listen to you⁺ rather than God, you⁺ must judge. <verse eid="ACT 4:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 4:20"/>For we are unable to stop speaking <char style="add">about</char> what we saw and heard.” <verse eid="ACT 4:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 4:21"/>And having further threatened <char style="add">them</char>, they let them go, finding no way they might punish them, on account of the people, because all were glorifying God for that having happened. <verse eid="ACT 4:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 4:22"/>For the man on whom this sign of healing had taken place was more than forty years <char style="add">old</char>. <verse eid="ACT 4:22"/></para>

<para style="s">The Believers’ PrayerPsalm 2:1–12</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 4:23"/>Now having been let go, they came to <char style="add">their</char> own and reported how much the chief priests and the elders had said to them. <verse eid="ACT 4:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 4:24"/>And having heard, they lifted up <char style="add">their</char> voice with one accord to God and said, “Sovereign Lord, You made<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.24 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">You are God, who made</char></note> the heaven and the earth and the sea and all that <char style="add">is</char> in them, <verse eid="ACT 4:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 4:25"/>having spoken by the Holy Spirit through the mouth of Your servant,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR do not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">by the Holy Spirit</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> our father David:<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">child</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verses 27 and 30</char></note> </para>

<para style="q1" vid="ACT 4:25">‘Why did the Gentiles rage </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 4:25">and the peoples devise vain things? <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Your servant David</char></note><verse eid="ACT 4:25"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 4:26"/>The kings of the earth took <char style="add">their</char> stand, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 4:26">and the rulers were gathered together </para>

<para style="q1" vid="ACT 4:26">against the Lord </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 4:26">and against His Christ.’<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.26 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">His Anointed One</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 4:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 4:27"/>For in truth, both Herod and Pontius Pilate, with the Gentiles and the peoples of Israel, were gathered together in this city<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.27 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR do not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in this city</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> against Your holy servant Jesus, whom You anointed, <verse eid="ACT 4:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 4:28"/>to do whatever Your hand and Your purpose predetermined to happen. <verse eid="ACT 4:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 4:29"/>And now, Lord, look upon their threats, and grant to Your servants to speak Your word with all boldness, <verse eid="ACT 4:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 4:30"/>while You stretch out Your hand for healing and signs and wonders to take place through the name of Your holy servant Jesus.” <verse eid="ACT 4:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 4:31"/>And <char style="add">on</char> their having prayed, the place in which they were assembled was shaken, and they were all filled with the Holy Spirit and were speaking the word of God with boldness. <verse eid="ACT 4:31"/></para>

<para style="s">Sharing among BelieversActs 2:42–47</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 4:32"/>Now the multitude of those having believed were one <char style="add">in</char> heart and soul, and no one claimed anything of that being his<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.32 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> RP </char><char style="fq" closed="false">theirs</char></note> to be his own, but all things were to them in common. <verse eid="ACT 4:32"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 4:33"/>And <char style="add">with</char> great power the apostles were giving testimony of the resurrection of the Lord Jesus, and great grace was upon them all. <verse eid="ACT 4:33"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 4:34"/>For there was not even anyone in need among them, for as many as were owners of lands or houses, selling <char style="add">them</char>, were bringing the proceeds of what is sold <verse eid="ACT 4:34"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 4:35"/>and were laying <char style="add">them</char> at the feet of the apostles, and distribution was made to each just as anyone had need. <verse eid="ACT 4:35"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 4:36"/>Now Joseph<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">4.36 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Joses</char></note> having been called Barnabas by the apostles (which is translated Son of Encouragement), a Levite, a Cypriot by birth, <verse eid="ACT 4:36"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 4:37"/>having sold a field being his, brought the money and laid <char style="add">it</char> at the feet of the apostles. <verse eid="ACT 4:37"/></para>

<chapter eid="ACT 4"/>

<chapter number="5" style="c" sid="ACT 5"/>

<para style="s">Ananias and Sapphira</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 5:1"/>Now a certain man named Ananias, with his wife Sapphira, sold a property, <verse eid="ACT 5:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 5:2"/>and he kept back from the proceeds, also the wife being aware of <char style="add">it</char>, and having brought a certain portion, he laid <char style="add">it</char> at the feet of the apostles. <verse eid="ACT 5:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 5:3"/>But Peter said, “Ananias, why did Satan fill your heart <char style="add">for</char> you to lie to the Holy Spirit and to keep back from the proceeds of the land? <verse eid="ACT 5:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 5:4"/>Remaining, did it not remain yours? And having been sold, was it <char style="add">not</char> in <char style="add">your</char> own authority? Why did you purpose this deed in your heart? You did not lie to men but to God!” <verse eid="ACT 5:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 5:5"/>And hearing these words, Ananias, having fallen down, breathed his last. And great fear came upon all those hearing. <verse eid="ACT 5:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 5:6"/>And the young ones, having arisen, wrapped him up, and having carried <char style="add">him</char> out, buried <char style="add">him</char>. <verse eid="ACT 5:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 5:7"/>Now it came to pass about three hours afterward <char style="add">that</char> his wife also came in, not knowing that having happened. <verse eid="ACT 5:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 5:8"/>And Peter responded to her, “Tell me if you⁺ sold the land for so much?” </para>

<para style="p" vid="ACT 5:8">And she said, “Yes, for so much.” <verse eid="ACT 5:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 5:9"/>But Peter <char style="add">said</char> to her, “Why <char style="add">is it</char> that you⁺ have agreed together to test the Spirit of the Lord? Behold, the feet of those having buried your husband <char style="add">are</char> at the door, and they will carry you out.” <verse eid="ACT 5:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 5:10"/>And immediately she fell down at his feet and breathed her last. And the young men, having come in, found her dead; and having carried <char style="add">her</char> out, they buried <char style="add">her</char> by her husband. <verse eid="ACT 5:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 5:11"/>And great fear came upon the whole church and upon all those hearing these things. <verse eid="ACT 5:11"/></para>

<para style="s">The Apostles Heal Many</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 5:12"/>Now by the hands of the apostles, many signs and wonders were happening among the people, and they were all with one accord in Solomon’s Colonnade. <verse eid="ACT 5:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 5:13"/>Now none of the rest dared to join them, but the people were magnifying them. <verse eid="ACT 5:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 5:14"/>And more believing in the Lord were added, multitudes of both men and women, <verse eid="ACT 5:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 5:15"/>so as even to bring out the sick into the streets and to put <char style="add">them</char> on cots and mats, so that of Peter coming, at least the shadow might envelop some of them. <verse eid="ACT 5:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 5:16"/>Now the multitude from the cities surrounding Jerusalem also were coming together, bringing the sick and <char style="add">those</char> being tormented by unclean spirits, who were all healed. <verse eid="ACT 5:16"/></para>

<para style="s">The Apostles Arrested and Freed</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 5:17"/>But the high priest, having risen up, and all those with him, being the sect of the Sadducees, were filled with jealousy, <verse eid="ACT 5:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 5:18"/>and they laid the hands on the apostles and put them in the public jail. <verse eid="ACT 5:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 5:19"/>But during the night an angel of the Lord, having opened the doors of the jail and having brought them out, said, <verse eid="ACT 5:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 5:20"/>“Go, and having stood in the temple,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the temple courts</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verses 21, 25, and 42</char></note> speak to the people all the words of this life.” <verse eid="ACT 5:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 5:21"/>And having heard, they entered into the temple at the dawn and were teaching. Now the high priest having come, and those with him, they called together the Council<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.21 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Sanhedrin</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verses 27, 34, and 41</char></note>—even all the senate of the sons of Israel—and they sent to the prison house to bring them. <verse eid="ACT 5:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 5:22"/>But the officers, having come, did not find them in the prison. And having returned, they reported back, <verse eid="ACT 5:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 5:23"/>saying, “We found<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.23 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">We indeed found</char></note> the prison house shut with all security and the guards standing before the doors; but having opened <char style="add">them</char>, we found no one inside.” <verse eid="ACT 5:23"/></para>

<para style="s">The Apostles before the Sanhedrin</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 5:24"/>Now when both the captain<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.24 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">when the high priest and the captain</char></note> of the temple and the chief priests heard these words, they were perplexed concerning them, what this might be.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.24 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">as to what was happening</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 5:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 5:25"/>And a certain one, having come, reported to them, “Behold, the men whom you⁺ put in the prison are standing in the temple and teaching the people!” <verse eid="ACT 5:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 5:26"/>Then the captain, having gone with the officers, was bringing them, not with force—for they were afraid of the people, lest they might be stoned. <verse eid="ACT 5:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 5:27"/>And having brought them, they set <char style="add">them</char> in the Council. And the high priest questioned them, <verse eid="ACT 5:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 5:28"/>saying, “By a charge we commanded you⁺ not to teach in this name, and behold, you⁺ have filled Jerusalem with your⁺ teaching, and you⁺ intend to bring upon us the blood of this man.” <verse eid="ACT 5:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 5:29"/>But Peter and the apostles, answering, said, “It is necessary to obey God rather than men. <verse eid="ACT 5:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 5:30"/>The God of our fathers raised up Jesus, whom you⁺ killed, having hanged <char style="add">Him</char> on a tree. <verse eid="ACT 5:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 5:31"/>God exalted Him to His right hand <char style="add">as</char> Prince and Savior to give repentance to Israel and forgiveness of sins. <verse eid="ACT 5:31"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 5:32"/>And we are witnesses<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.32 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">His witnesses</char></note> of these things, and also the Holy Spirit, whom God has given to those obeying Him.” <verse eid="ACT 5:32"/></para>

<para style="s">Gamaliel’s Advice</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 5:33"/>And having heard, they were cut, and they were intending<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.33 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> ECM, BYZ, TR, and Tischendorf </char><char style="fq" closed="false">they were resolving</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">they were taking counsel</char></note> to put them to death. <verse eid="ACT 5:33"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 5:34"/>But a certain <char style="add">man</char> having risen up in the Council, a Pharisee named Gamaliel, a teacher of the law honored by all the people, commanded <char style="add">them</char> to put the men<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.34 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the apostles</char></note> outside for a short while. <verse eid="ACT 5:34"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 5:35"/>And he said to them, “Men, Israelites, take heed to yourselves what you⁺ are about to do with these men. <verse eid="ACT 5:35"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 5:36"/>For before these days, Theudas rose up, affirming himself to be somebody—to whom a number of men, about four hundred, were joined—who was put to death, and all, as many as were persuaded by him, were dispersed; and it came to nothing. <verse eid="ACT 5:36"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 5:37"/>After this man, Judas the Galilean rose up in the days of the registration and drew away people<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.37 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">many people</char></note> after him. And he perished, and all, as many as were persuaded by him, were scattered. <verse eid="ACT 5:37"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 5:38"/>And now I say to you⁺, withdraw from these men and let them alone, for if this purpose or this work may be from men, it will be overthrown. <verse eid="ACT 5:38"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="ACT 5:39"/>But if it is from God, you⁺ will not be able to overthrow them,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.39 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to overthrow it</char></note> lest perhaps you⁺ would be found fighting against God.” <verse eid="ACT 5:39"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="ACT 5:40"/>And they were persuaded by him. And having summoned the apostles, having beaten <char style="add">them</char>, they commanded <char style="add">them</char> not to speak in the name of Jesus, and they released <char style="add">them</char>. <verse eid="ACT 5:40"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="ACT 5:41"/>Therefore they indeed departed from the presence of the Council, rejoicing that they had been counted worthy to suffer dishonor for the Name.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">5.41 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">for the name of Jesus</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">for His name</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; F35 </char><char style="fq" closed="false">for the name of the Christ</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 5:41"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="ACT 5:42"/>And every day, in the temple and in the house, they did not cease teaching and proclaiming the good news <char style="add">that</char> Jesus <char style="add">is</char> the Christ. <verse eid="ACT 5:42"/></para>

<chapter eid="ACT 5"/>

<chapter number="6" style="c" sid="ACT 6"/>

<para style="s">The Choosing of the Seven</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 6:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">1 Timothy 3:8–13</char></note>Now in these days of the disciples multiplying, there arose a grumbling of the Hellenists against the Hebrews,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Grecian Jews among them began to grumble against the Hebraic Jews</char></note> because their widows were being overlooked in the daily distribution. <verse eid="ACT 6:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 6:2"/>So the Twelve, having summoned the multitude of the disciples, said, “It is not desirable <char style="add">for</char> us, having neglected the word of God, to attend tables. <verse eid="ACT 6:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 6:3"/>Therefore, brothers, select from yourselves seven men being well attested, full of the Spirit<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Holy Spirit</char></note> and of wisdom, whom we will appoint over this task. <verse eid="ACT 6:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 6:4"/>And we will steadfastly continue in prayer and the ministry of the word.” <verse eid="ACT 6:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 6:5"/>And the statement was pleasing before all the multitude. And they chose Stephen, a man full of faith and <char style="add">of</char> the Holy Spirit, and Philip, and Prochorus, and Nicanor, and Timon, and Parmenas, and Nicolas, a convert of Antioch, <verse eid="ACT 6:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 6:6"/>whom they set before the apostles. And having prayed, they laid the hands on them. <verse eid="ACT 6:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 6:7"/>And the word of God kept increasing, and the number of the disciples in Jerusalem was multiplied exceedingly, and a great multitude of the priests were becoming obedient to the faith. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> GOC </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of the Jews</char></note><verse eid="ACT 6:7"/></para>

<para style="s">The Arrest of Stephen</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 6:8"/>Now Stephen, full of grace<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of faith</char></note> and power, was doing great wonders and signs among the people. <verse eid="ACT 6:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 6:9"/>But there arose certain ones of those of the synagogue called Freedmen—including Cyrenians and Alexandrians and those from Cilicia and Asia—<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and men from the provinces of Cilicia and Asia</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; the Roman province of Asia was located in what is now western Turkey.</char></note> disputing with Stephen. <verse eid="ACT 6:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 6:10"/>And they were not able to withstand the wisdom and the Spirit by whom he was speaking. <verse eid="ACT 6:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 6:11"/>Then they suborned men to say, “We have heard him speaking blasphemous words against Moses and God.” <verse eid="ACT 6:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 6:12"/>And they stirred up the people and the elders and the scribes; and having come upon <char style="add">him</char>, they seized him and brought <char style="add">him</char> to the Council.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Sanhedrin</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verse 15</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 6:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 6:13"/>And they set up false witnesses, saying, “This man does not stop speaking words<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">6.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">words of blasphemy</char></note> against this holy place and the law. <verse eid="ACT 6:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 6:14"/>For we have heard him saying that this Jesus of Nazareth will demolish this place and will change the customs that Moses delivered to us.” <verse eid="ACT 6:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 6:15"/>And having looked intently on him, all the ones sitting in the Council saw his face as the face of an angel. <verse eid="ACT 6:15"/></para>

<chapter eid="ACT 6"/>

<chapter number="7" style="c" sid="ACT 7"/>

<para style="s">Stephen’s Address: The Call of Abraham</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 7:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Genesis 12:1–9</char></note>And the high priest said, “Are these things so?” <verse eid="ACT 7:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 7:2"/>And he began to speak: “Men, brothers and fathers, listen! The God of glory appeared to our father Abraham, being in Mesopotamia before his dwelling in Haran, <verse eid="ACT 7:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 7:3"/>and He said to him, ‘Go out of your country and from your kindred, and come into the land that I will show to you.’ <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Genesis 12:1</char></note><verse eid="ACT 7:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 7:4"/>Then, having gone out from the land of the Chaldeans, he dwelt in Haran. And from there, after his father died, He transferred him into this land in which you⁺ now dwell. <verse eid="ACT 7:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 7:5"/>And He did not give to him an inheritance in it, not even the length of a foot; but He promised to give it to him for a possession, and to his seed after him—there being to him no child. <verse eid="ACT 7:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 7:6"/>And God spoke thus, that his seed will be a sojourner in a strange land, and they will enslave it and will mistreat <char style="add">it</char> four hundred years. <verse eid="ACT 7:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 7:7"/>‘And the nation to which they will be in bondage, I will judge,’ God said, ‘and after these things they will come out and will serve Me in this place.’ <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Genesis 15:13–14; Exodus 3:12</char></note><verse eid="ACT 7:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 7:8"/>And He gave to him the covenant of circumcision; and thus he begat Isaac and circumcised him on the eighth day, and Isaac Jacob, and Jacob the twelve patriarchs. <verse eid="ACT 7:8"/></para>

<para style="s">Joseph Sold into EgyptGenesis 37:12–30</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 7:9"/>And the patriarchs, having envied Joseph, sold <char style="add">him</char> into Egypt. And God was with him, <verse eid="ACT 7:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 7:10"/>and He rescued him out of all his tribulations, and He gave him favor and wisdom before Pharaoh king of Egypt, and he appointed him ruler over Egypt and over all his house. <verse eid="ACT 7:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 7:11"/>And there was a famine upon all<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the land of</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> Egypt and Canaan, and great affliction, and our fathers were not finding sustenance. <verse eid="ACT 7:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 7:12"/>Now Jacob, having heard <char style="add">there</char> is grain in Egypt, sent forth our fathers first. <verse eid="ACT 7:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 7:13"/>And on the second time, Joseph was made known to<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Joseph was recognized by</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Joseph revealed himself to</char></note> his brothers, and the family of Joseph became known to Pharaoh. <verse eid="ACT 7:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 7:14"/>And Joseph, having sent, called for his father Jacob and all <char style="add">his</char> kindred, seventy-five souls in all. <verse eid="ACT 7:14"/></para>

<para style="s">Israel Oppressed in EgyptExodus 1:8–22</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 7:15"/>And Jacob went down into Egypt, and he died—he and our fathers, <verse eid="ACT 7:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 7:16"/>and they were carried over<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Their bones were carried back</char></note> into Shechem and were placed in the tomb that Abraham bought for a price of silver from the sons of Hamor in Shechem.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of Shechem</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 7:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 7:17"/>Now as the time of the promise that God swore to Abraham was drawing near, the people increased and multiplied in Egypt, <verse eid="ACT 7:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 7:18"/>until there arose another king over Egypt,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.18 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR do not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">over Egypt</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> who did not know Joseph. <verse eid="ACT 7:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 7:19"/>Having dealt treacherously with our kindred, this one mistreated our fathers, making <char style="add">them</char> expose their infants, that they would not live. <verse eid="ACT 7:19"/></para>

<para style="s">The Birth and Adoption of MosesExodus 2:1–10</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 7:20"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Hebrews 11:23–29</char></note>In that time Moses was born (and he was beautiful to God),<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">he was of great status to God</char></note> who was brought up three months in the house of <char style="add">his</char> father. <verse eid="ACT 7:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 7:21"/>And <char style="add">on</char> his having been exposed, the daughter of Pharaoh took him up and brought him up for herself for a son. <verse eid="ACT 7:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 7:22"/>And Moses was educated in all the wisdom of the Egyptians, and he was mighty in his words and deeds. <verse eid="ACT 7:22"/></para>

<para style="s">The Rejection and Flight of MosesExodus 2:11–22</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 7:23"/>Now when a period of forty years was fulfilled to him, it came into his heart to visit his brothers, the sons of Israel. <verse eid="ACT 7:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 7:24"/>And having seen a certain one being wronged, he defended and did vengeance for the one being oppressed, having struck down the Egyptian. <verse eid="ACT 7:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 7:25"/>And he was supposing his brothers to understand that God is giving them salvation by his hand, but they did not understand. <verse eid="ACT 7:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 7:26"/>And on the following day, he appeared to those who were quarreling and urged them to peace, having said, ‘Men, you⁺ are brothers. Why do you⁺ wrong one another?’ <verse eid="ACT 7:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 7:27"/>But the one mistreating the neighbor pushed him away, having said, ‘Who appointed you ruler and judge over us? <verse eid="ACT 7:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 7:28"/>Do you want to kill me the same way you killed the Egyptian yesterday?’ <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.28 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Exodus 2:13–14 (see also LXX)</char></note><verse eid="ACT 7:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 7:29"/>Now at this word Moses fled, and he became a sojourner in the land of Midian, where he begat two sons. <verse eid="ACT 7:29"/></para>

<para style="s">The Call of MosesExodus 3:1–22</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 7:30"/>And forty years having been fulfilled, an angel<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.30 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Angel</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verses 35 and 38; BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of the Lord</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> appeared to him in the wilderness of Mount Sinai, in a flame of fire of a bush. <verse eid="ACT 7:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 7:31"/>And Moses, having seen, marveled at the vision. And <char style="add">on</char> his coming near to behold, there was the voice of the Lord:<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.31 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to him</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 7:31"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 7:32"/>‘I <char style="add">am</char> the God of your fathers, the God of Abraham and of Isaac and of Jacob.’ And Moses, having become terrified, did not dare to look. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.32 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Exodus 3:6</char></note><verse eid="ACT 7:32"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 7:33"/>And the Lord said to him, ‘Loose the sandal of your feet, for the place on which you stand is holy ground. <verse eid="ACT 7:33"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 7:34"/>I have surely seen the oppression of My people in Egypt, and I heard their groans, and I came down to deliver them. And now come, I will send you to Egypt.’ <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.34 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Exodus 3:5–10</char></note><verse eid="ACT 7:34"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 7:35"/>This Moses, whom they rejected, having said, ‘Who appointed you ruler and judge?’— this one whom God sent <char style="add">as</char> both ruler and redeemer by the hand of the angel having appeared to him in the bush— <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.35 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Exodus 2:14</char></note><verse eid="ACT 7:35"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 7:36"/>this one led them out, having done wonders and signs in the land of Egypt, and in the Red Sea, and in the wilderness<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.36 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">desert</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verses 38, 42, and 44</char></note> forty years. <verse eid="ACT 7:36"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 7:37"/>This is the Moses having said to the sons of Israel, ‘God will raise up<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.37 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ </char><char style="fq" closed="false">The Lord our God will raise up</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">The Lord your God will raise up</char></note> for you⁺ a prophet like me from among your⁺ brothers.’<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.37 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Deuteronomy 18:15</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 7:37"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 7:38"/>This is the one having been in the congregation in the wilderness with the angel speaking to him in Mount Sinai, and <char style="add">with</char> our fathers, who received living oracles<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.38 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ </char><char style="fq" closed="false">a living word</char></note> to give to us,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.38 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> NE and WH </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to you</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 7:38"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="ACT 7:39"/>to whom our fathers were not willing to be obedient, but pushed away, and they turned back in their hearts to Egypt, <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.39 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ </char><char style="fq" closed="false">heart</char></note><verse eid="ACT 7:39"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="ACT 7:40"/>having said to Aaron, ‘Make us gods who will go before us. As for this Moses, who brought us out from the land of Egypt, we do not know what happened to him.’ <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.40 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Exodus 32:1</char></note><verse eid="ACT 7:40"/></para>

<para style="s">The Rebellion of Israel</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="ACT 7:41"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Amos 5:16–27</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Deuteronomy 9:7–29</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Exodus 32:1–35</char></note>And in those days they made a calf and offered a sacrifice to the idol, and they were rejoicing in the works of their hands. <verse eid="ACT 7:41"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="ACT 7:42"/>But God turned away and delivered them to worship the host of heaven, as it has been written in the book of the prophets: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="ACT 7:42">‘Did you⁺ offer slain beasts and sacrifices to Me </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 7:42">forty years in the wilderness, O house of Israel? <verse eid="ACT 7:42"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="ACT 7:43"/>And you⁺ took up the tabernacle of Molech </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 7:43">and the star of your⁺ god Rephan, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 7:43">the images that you⁺ made to worship them; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="ACT 7:43">and I will remove you⁺ </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 7:43">beyond Babylon.’<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.43 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> RP </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Remphan</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; F35 </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Rephphan</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; WH </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Rompha</char></note> <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.43 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Amos 5:25–27 (see also LXX)</char></note><verse eid="ACT 7:43"/></para>

<para style="s">The Tabernacle of the TestimonyExodus 40:1–33</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="44" style="v" sid="ACT 7:44"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Hebrews 9:1–10</char></note>The tabernacle of the Testimony was with our fathers in the wilderness, just as the One speaking to Moses had commanded <char style="add">him</char> to make it according to the pattern that he had seen, <verse eid="ACT 7:44"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="45" style="v" sid="ACT 7:45"/>and which, having received <char style="add">it</char> by succession, our fathers brought in with Joshua in taking possession of the nations whom God drove out from the face of our fathers, until the days of David, <verse eid="ACT 7:45"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="46" style="v" sid="ACT 7:46"/>who found favor before God and asked to find a dwelling place for the God of Jacob. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.46 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> SBL, WH, BYZ, and TR; see also LXX for Psalm 132:5; ECM, NA, and NE </char><char style="fq" closed="false">a dwelling place for the house of Jacob.</char></note><verse eid="ACT 7:46"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="47" style="v" sid="ACT 7:47"/>But Solomon built for Him a house. <verse eid="ACT 7:47"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="48" style="v" sid="ACT 7:48"/>But the Most High does not dwell in hand-made <char style="add">houses</char>.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.48 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">temples made by hands</char></note> As the prophet says: <verse eid="ACT 7:48"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="49" style="v" sid="ACT 7:49"/>‘Heaven <char style="add">is</char> unto Me a throne, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 7:49">and the earth a footstool for My feet. </para>

<para style="q1" vid="ACT 7:49">What kind of house will you⁺ build for Me, says the Lord, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 7:49">or what <char style="add">is</char> the place of My rest? <verse eid="ACT 7:49"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="50" style="v" sid="ACT 7:50"/>Did not My hand make all these things?’ <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.50 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Isaiah 66:1–2</char></note><verse eid="ACT 7:50"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="51" style="v" sid="ACT 7:51"/>You⁺ stiff-necked and uncircumcised in hearts<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.51 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">heart</char></note> and ears! You⁺ always resist the Holy Spirit! As <char style="add">did</char> your⁺ fathers, also you⁺ <char style="add">do</char>. <verse eid="ACT 7:51"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="52" style="v" sid="ACT 7:52"/>Which of the prophets did your⁺ fathers not persecute? And they killed those having foretold about the coming of the Righteous One, of whom you⁺ have now become betrayers and murderers, <verse eid="ACT 7:52"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="53" style="v" sid="ACT 7:53"/><char style="add">you</char> who received the law by the ordination of angels, and did not keep <char style="add">it</char>.” <verse eid="ACT 7:53"/></para>

<para style="s">The Stoning of Stephen</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="54" style="v" sid="ACT 7:54"/>Now hearing these things, they were cut in their hearts,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">7.54 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">On hearing this, they were enraged,</char></note> and they were gnashing the teeth at him. <verse eid="ACT 7:54"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="55" style="v" sid="ACT 7:55"/>But being full of the Holy Spirit, having looked intently into heaven, he saw the glory of God and Jesus standing at the right hand of God, <verse eid="ACT 7:55"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="56" style="v" sid="ACT 7:56"/>and he said, “Behold, I see the heavens having been opened and the Son of Man standing at the right hand of God.” <verse eid="ACT 7:56"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="57" style="v" sid="ACT 7:57"/>And having cried out in a loud voice, they held their ears and rushed upon him with one accord, <verse eid="ACT 7:57"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="58" style="v" sid="ACT 7:58"/>and having cast <char style="add">him</char> out of the city, they began to stone <char style="add">him</char>. And the witnesses laid aside their garments at the feet of a young man named Saul. <verse eid="ACT 7:58"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="59" style="v" sid="ACT 7:59"/>And <char style="add">as</char> they were stoning Stephen, he was calling out and saying, “Lord Jesus, receive my spirit.” <verse eid="ACT 7:59"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="60" style="v" sid="ACT 7:60"/>And having fallen on <char style="add">his</char> knees, he cried out in a loud voice, “Lord, do not place this sin on them.” And having said this, he fell asleep. <verse eid="ACT 7:60"/></para>

<chapter eid="ACT 7"/>

<chapter number="8" style="c" sid="ACT 8"/>

<para style="s">Saul Persecutes the Church</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 8:1"/>And Saul was there consenting to his killing. And on that day a great persecution arose against the church that <char style="add">was</char> in Jerusalem, and all except the apostles were scattered throughout the regions of Judea and Samaria. <verse eid="ACT 8:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 8:2"/>Now devout men buried Stephen and made great lamentation over him. <verse eid="ACT 8:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 8:3"/>But Saul was destroying the church. Entering into the houses and dragging off men and women, he was delivering <char style="add">them</char> to prison. <verse eid="ACT 8:3"/></para>

<para style="s">Philip in Samaria</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 8:4"/>Then indeed those having been scattered went about preaching the word. <verse eid="ACT 8:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 8:5"/>Now Philip, having gone down to a city of Samaria,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the city of Samaria</char></note> was proclaiming the Christ to them. <verse eid="ACT 8:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 8:6"/>And the crowds, with one accord, were giving heed to the things being spoken by Philip in their hearing and seeing the signs that he was performing. <verse eid="ACT 8:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 8:7"/>For <char style="add">from</char> many of those having unclean spirits they were coming out, crying in a loud voice. And many having been paralyzed and lame were healed. <verse eid="ACT 8:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 8:8"/>So there was great joy in that city. <verse eid="ACT 8:8"/></para>

<para style="s">Simon the SorcererDeuteronomy 18:9–14</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 8:9"/>Now a certain man named Simon had been formerly practicing sorcery in the city and amazing the people of Samaria, declaring himself to be someone great, <verse eid="ACT 8:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 8:10"/>to whom they were all<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> RP does not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">all</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> giving heed, from small to great, saying, “This one is the power of God that <char style="add">is</char> called Great.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Great Power of God</char></note>” <verse eid="ACT 8:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 8:11"/>Now they were giving heed to him because for a long time he had amazed them with the magic arts. <verse eid="ACT 8:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 8:12"/>But when they believed Philip proclaiming the gospel concerning the kingdom of God and the name of Jesus Christ, they were baptized, both men and women. <verse eid="ACT 8:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 8:13"/>And Simon himself also believed, and having been baptized, he was steadfastly continuing with Philip. And beholding the signs and great miracles<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and Scrivener TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the miracles and signs</char></note> being performed, he was amazed. <verse eid="ACT 8:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 8:14"/>Now the apostles in Jerusalem, having heard that Samaria had received the word of God, sent to them Peter and John, <verse eid="ACT 8:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 8:15"/>who, having come down, prayed for them, that they might receive the Holy Spirit. <verse eid="ACT 8:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 8:16"/>For He was not yet fallen upon any of them, but they had only been baptized into the name of the Lord Jesus.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of the Lord Jesus Christ</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 8:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 8:17"/>Then they began laying the hands upon them, and they received the Holy Spirit. <verse eid="ACT 8:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 8:18"/>Now Simon, having seen that the Spirit<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.18 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Holy Spirit</char></note> was given through the laying on of the apostles’ hands, offered to them money, <verse eid="ACT 8:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 8:19"/>saying, “Give also to me this authority, so that on whomever I may lay the hands, he may receive the Holy Spirit.” <verse eid="ACT 8:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 8:20"/>But Peter said to him, “Your silver with you, may it be to destruction, because you thought the gift of God was to be obtained by money! <verse eid="ACT 8:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 8:21"/>To you there is no part nor lot in this matter, for your heart is not right before God.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.21 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in the sight of God</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 8:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 8:22"/>Repent, therefore, of this wickedness of yours, and pray earnestly to the Lord,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to God</char></note> if indeed the intent of your heart will be forgiven you. <verse eid="ACT 8:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 8:23"/>For I see you being in the gall of bitterness and the bond of iniquity.” <verse eid="ACT 8:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 8:24"/>And Simon, answering, said, “You⁺ pray earnestly to the Lord<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.24 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> GOC </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Pray to God</char></note> on behalf of me, so that nothing of which you⁺ have spoken may come upon me.” <verse eid="ACT 8:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 8:25"/>Then they indeed, having earnestly testified and having spoken the word of the Lord, traveled back to Jerusalem, and they were preaching the gospel to many villages of the Samaritans. <verse eid="ACT 8:25"/></para>

<para style="s">Philip and the EthiopianIsaiah 53:1–8</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 8:26"/>Now an angel of the Lord spoke to Philip, saying, “Rise up and go toward the south, to the road going down from Jerusalem to Gaza.” (This is desert.) <verse eid="ACT 8:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 8:27"/>And having risen up, he went. And behold, a man, an Ethiopian eunuch, a potentate of Kandake, queen<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.27 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Candace, queen</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Candace, the queen</char></note> of the Ethiopians, who was over all her treasure, who had come to Jerusalem to worship. <verse eid="ACT 8:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 8:28"/>And he was returning and sitting in his chariot, and he was reading the prophet Isaiah. <verse eid="ACT 8:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 8:29"/>And the Spirit said to Philip, “Go near and join yourself to this chariot.” <verse eid="ACT 8:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 8:30"/>And Philip, having run up, heard him reading Isaiah the prophet, and he said, “Do you then understand what you are reading?” <verse eid="ACT 8:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 8:31"/>And he said, “How indeed could I be able, unless someone will guide me?” And he invited Philip, having come up, to sit with him. <verse eid="ACT 8:31"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 8:32"/>Now the passage of Scripture that he was reading was this: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="ACT 8:32">“He was led as a sheep to slaughter, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 8:32">and as a lamb before the one shearing it <char style="add">is</char> silent, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 8:32">so He does not open His mouth. <verse eid="ACT 8:32"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 8:33"/>In His humiliation, justice was taken away from Him. </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 8:33">Who will describe His generation? </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 8:33">For His life is removed from the earth.” <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.33 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Isaiah 53:7–8 (see also LXX)</char></note><verse eid="ACT 8:33"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 8:34"/>And the eunuch, answering, said to Philip, “I beseech you, about whom does the prophet say this? About himself, or about some other?” <verse eid="ACT 8:34"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 8:35"/>And Philip, having opened his mouth and having begun from this Scripture, proclaimed the good news to him—Jesus. <verse eid="ACT 8:35"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 8:36"/>And as they were going along the road, they came upon some water, and the eunuch says, “Behold, water! What prevents my being baptized?”<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">8.36 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> TR includes </char><char style="fq" closed="false">37</char><char style="fq" closed="false">And Philip said, “If you believe out of all the heart, it is lawful.” And he answered, “I believe the Son of God to be Jesus Christ.”</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 8:36"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 8:38"/>And he commanded the chariot to stop. And they both went down to the water—both Philip and the eunuch—and he baptized him. <verse eid="ACT 8:38"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="ACT 8:39"/>Now when they came up out of the water, the Spirit of the Lord carried away Philip, and the eunuch saw him no longer. For he went on his way rejoicing. <verse eid="ACT 8:39"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="ACT 8:40"/>But Philip was found at Azotus, and passing through, he was proclaiming the gospel to all the towns until his coming to Caesarea. <verse eid="ACT 8:40"/></para>

<chapter eid="ACT 8"/>

<chapter number="9" style="c" sid="ACT 9"/>

<para style="s">The Road to Damascus</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 9:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Acts 26:1–23</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Acts 22:1–21</char></note>Now Saul, still breathing out threats and murder toward the disciples of the Lord, having gone to the high priest, <verse eid="ACT 9:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 9:2"/>requested letters from him to the synagogues in Damascus, so that if he found any being of the Way, both men and women, having bound <char style="add">them</char>, he might bring <char style="add">them</char> to Jerusalem. <verse eid="ACT 9:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 9:3"/>Now in going, it came to pass <char style="add">that</char> he drew near to Damascus, and suddenly a light from heaven flashed around him. <verse eid="ACT 9:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 9:4"/>And having fallen on the ground, he heard a voice saying to him, <char style="wj">“Saul, Saul, why do you persecute Me?”</char> <verse eid="ACT 9:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 9:5"/>And he said, “Who are You, Lord?” And <char style="add">He said</char>,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">And the Lord replied</char></note> <char style="wj">“I am Jesus, whom you are persecuting.</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> TR includes </char><char style="fq" closed="false">“It is hard for you to kick against the goads.” </char><char style="fq" closed="false">6</char><char style="fq" closed="false">And trembling and astonished, the man asked, “Lord, what do You want me to do?” And the Lord said to him:</char></note><char style="wj"> </char><verse eid="ACT 9:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 9:6"/><char style="wj">“But rise up and enter into the city, and it will be told to you that which it is necessary for you to do.”</char> <verse eid="ACT 9:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 9:7"/>And the men traveling with him stood speechless, hearing the voice indeed, but seeing no one. <verse eid="ACT 9:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 9:8"/>And Saul rose up from the ground, but his eyes having been opened, he could see nothing. And leading him by the hand, they brought <char style="add">him</char> to Damascus. <verse eid="ACT 9:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 9:9"/>And he was three days without seeing, and he did not eat, nor did he drink. <verse eid="ACT 9:9"/></para>

<para style="s">Ananias Baptizes Saul</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 9:10"/>Now there was a certain disciple in Damascus named Ananias. And the Lord said to him in a vision, <char style="wj">“Ananias!”</char> </para>

<para style="p" vid="ACT 9:10">And he said, “Behold, <char style="add">it is</char> I, Lord.” <verse eid="ACT 9:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 9:11"/>And the Lord <char style="add">said</char> to him, <char style="wj">“Having risen up, go into the street called Straight, and seek in the house of Judas the one of Tarsus named Saul, for behold, he is praying, </char><verse eid="ACT 9:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 9:12"/><char style="wj">and he saw in a vision</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> ECM does not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in a vision</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note><char style="wj"> a man named Ananias having come and having put the hands</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">a hand</char></note><char style="wj"> on him so that he might see again.”</char> <verse eid="ACT 9:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 9:13"/>But Ananias answered, “Lord, I have heard from many concerning this man, how many evils he did to Your saints in Jerusalem. <verse eid="ACT 9:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 9:14"/>And here he has authority from the chief priests to bind all those calling on Your name.” <verse eid="ACT 9:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 9:15"/>But the Lord said to him, <char style="wj">“Go, for this man is to Me a vessel of choice to carry My name before the Gentiles, and also kings and the sons of Israel. </char><verse eid="ACT 9:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 9:16"/><char style="wj">For I will show to him how much it is necessary for him to suffer for My name.”</char> <verse eid="ACT 9:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 9:17"/>And Ananias went away and entered into the house; and having laid the hands upon him, he said, “Brother Saul, the Lord Jesus,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Lord</char></note> the One having appeared to you on the road by which you were coming, has sent me so that you may see again and may be filled with the Holy Spirit.” <verse eid="ACT 9:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 9:18"/>And immediately <char style="add">something</char> like scales fell from his eyes, and he saw again.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.18 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> ALT, F35, and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">immediately</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> And having risen up, he was baptized, <verse eid="ACT 9:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 9:19"/>and having taken food, he was strengthened. And he was<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Saul was</char></note> some days with the disciples in Damascus. <verse eid="ACT 9:19"/></para>

<para style="s">Saul Preaches at Damascus</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 9:20"/>And immediately he began proclaiming Jesus<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> RP and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Christ</char></note> in the synagogues, that He is the Son of God. <verse eid="ACT 9:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 9:21"/>And all those hearing were amazed and were saying, “Is this not the one having ravaged those in Jerusalem calling on this name? And he had come here for this, so that he might bring them, having been bound, to the chief priests.” <verse eid="ACT 9:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 9:22"/>But Saul was empowered all the more and kept confounding the Jews dwelling in Damascus, proving that this is the Christ. <verse eid="ACT 9:22"/></para>

<para style="s">The Escape from Damascus</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 9:23"/>Now when many days had passed, the Jews plotted together to kill him, <verse eid="ACT 9:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 9:24"/>but their plot became known to Saul. And now they were closely watching the gates day and also night so that they might kill him. <verse eid="ACT 9:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 9:25"/>But having taken <char style="add">him</char> by night, his disciples<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the disciples</char></note> let him down through the wall,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">through a window in the wall</char></note> having lowered <char style="add">him</char> in a basket. <verse eid="ACT 9:25"/></para>

<para style="s">Saul in Jerusalem</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 9:26"/>And having arrived in Jerusalem, he was attempting to join the disciples, and all were afraid of him, not believing that he is a disciple. <verse eid="ACT 9:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 9:27"/>But Barnabas, having taken him, brought <char style="add">him</char> to the apostles and related to them how he had seen the Lord on the road, and that He had spoken to him, and how in Damascus he had spoken boldly in the name of Jesus.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.27 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> F35 </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Lord Jesus</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 9:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 9:28"/>And he was coming in and going out with them in Jerusalem, speaking boldly in the name of the Lord.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.28 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in the name of the Lord Jesus</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; F35 </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in the name of Jesus</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 9:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 9:29"/>And he was speaking and was debating with the Hellenists,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.29 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Grecian Jews</char></note> but they were seeking to kill him. <verse eid="ACT 9:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 9:30"/>But the brothers, having known, brought him down to Caesarea and sent him away to Tarsus. <verse eid="ACT 9:30"/></para>

<para style="s">The Healing of Aeneas</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 9:31"/>Then indeed the church<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.31 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">churches</char></note> throughout all of Judea and Galilee and Samaria had peace, being edified. And going on in the fear of the Lord and in the comfort of the Holy Spirit, they were multiplied. <verse eid="ACT 9:31"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 9:32"/>Now it came to pass <char style="add">that</char> Peter, passing through all <char style="add">quarters</char>, also went down to the saints inhabiting Lydda. <verse eid="ACT 9:32"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 9:33"/>And he found there a certain man named Aeneas, who was paralyzed, lying on a bed for eight years. <verse eid="ACT 9:33"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 9:34"/>And Peter said to him, “Aeneas, Jesus Christ heals you; rise up and make the bed for yourself.” And immediately he rose up, <verse eid="ACT 9:34"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 9:35"/>and all those inhabiting Lydda and Sharon saw him <char style="add">and</char> turned to the Lord. <verse eid="ACT 9:35"/></para>

<para style="s">The Raising of TabithaJohn 11:38–44</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 9:36"/>Now in Joppa there was a certain disciple named Tabitha (which, translated, is called Dorcas).<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.36 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Tabitha</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> in Aramaic and </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Dorcas</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> in Greek both mean </char><char style="fq" closed="false">gazelle</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> She was full of good works and of alms that she continually did. <verse eid="ACT 9:36"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 9:37"/>But in those days it came to pass <char style="add">that</char> having become sick, she died. And having washed <char style="add">her</char>, they put <char style="add">her</char> in an upper room.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.37 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> F35 </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the upper room</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 9:37"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 9:38"/>Now Lydda being near Joppa, the disciples, having heard that Peter is in it, sent two men<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.38 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ does not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">two men</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> to him, imploring, “Do not delay to come to us.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">9.38 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">imploring him not to delay in coming to them</char></note>” <verse eid="ACT 9:38"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="ACT 9:39"/>And Peter, having risen up, went with them, who, having arrived, brought <char style="add">him</char> into the upper room. And all the widows stood by him, weeping and showing the tunics and garments that Dorcas had made <char style="add">while</char> being with them. <verse eid="ACT 9:39"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="ACT 9:40"/>And Peter, having put all outside and having bowed the knees, prayed. And having turned to the body he said, “Tabitha, arise!” And she opened her eyes, and having seen Peter, she sat up. <verse eid="ACT 9:40"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="ACT 9:41"/>And having given her <char style="add">his</char> hand, he raised her up. And having called the saints and the widows, he presented her being alive. <verse eid="ACT 9:41"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="ACT 9:42"/>And it became known throughout all of Joppa, and many believed on the Lord. <verse eid="ACT 9:42"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="ACT 9:43"/>And it came to pass <char style="add">that</char> he stayed many days in Joppa with a certain Simon, a tanner. <verse eid="ACT 9:43"/></para>

<chapter eid="ACT 9"/>

<chapter number="10" style="c" sid="ACT 10"/>

<para style="s">Cornelius Sends for Peter</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 10:1"/>Now a certain man in Caesarea named Cornelius <char style="add">was</char> a centurion of the cohort that is called Italian, <verse eid="ACT 10:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 10:2"/>devout and fearing God with all his household, doing many alms to the people and praying to God through all. <verse eid="ACT 10:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 10:3"/>He saw clearly in a vision, as it was about the ninth hour of the day,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, about three in the afternoon; also in verse 30</char></note> an angel of God having come to him and having said to him, “Cornelius!” <verse eid="ACT 10:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 10:4"/>And having looked intently at him, and having become afraid, he said, “What is it, Lord?” And he said to him, “Your prayers and your alms have ascended as a memorial before God. <verse eid="ACT 10:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 10:5"/>And now send men to Joppa and summon a certain Simon,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and summon Simon</char></note> who is called Peter. <verse eid="ACT 10:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 10:6"/>He lodges with a certain Simon, a tanner whose house is by the sea.”<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> TR includes </char><char style="fq" closed="false">He will speak to you what it is necessary for you to do.</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 10:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 10:7"/>And when the angel speaking to him went away, having called two of the servants and a devout soldier of those attending him, <verse eid="ACT 10:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 10:8"/>and having related all things to them, he sent them to Joppa. <verse eid="ACT 10:8"/></para>

<para style="s">Peter’s VisionLeviticus 11:1–47</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 10:9"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Deuteronomy 14:1–21</char></note>Now on the next day, <char style="add">in</char> their journeying and approaching the city, Peter went up on the housetop about the sixth hour<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, about noon</char></note> to pray. <verse eid="ACT 10:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 10:10"/>And he became hungry and desired to eat. But <char style="add">in</char> their preparing, a trance fell upon him, <verse eid="ACT 10:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 10:11"/>and he sees heaven opening and a certain vessel as a great sheet descending, being let down upon the earth by four corners,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">upon the earth, bound at its four corners</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 10:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 10:12"/>in which were all the quadrupeds<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and wild beasts</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> and creeping things of the earth and birds of heaven. <verse eid="ACT 10:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 10:13"/>And a voice came to him: <char style="wj">“Having risen up, Peter, kill and eat!”</char> <verse eid="ACT 10:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 10:14"/>But Peter said, “In no way, Lord! For never have I eaten anything common<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">impure</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; similarly in verses 15 and 28</char></note> or unclean.” <verse eid="ACT 10:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 10:15"/>And a voice <char style="add">came</char> again to him for the second time: <char style="wj">“What God has cleansed, you do not call common.”</char> <verse eid="ACT 10:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 10:16"/>Now this took place for three times, and immediately<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and again</char></note> the vessel was taken up into heaven. <verse eid="ACT 10:16"/></para>

<para style="s">Peter Called to Caesarea</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 10:17"/>And while Peter was perplexed in himself <char style="add">as to</char> what the vision that he had seen might be, behold, the men having been sent from Cornelius, having inquired for the house of Simon, stood at the gate. <verse eid="ACT 10:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 10:18"/>And having called out, they were asking if Simon who <char style="add">is</char> called Peter is lodged here. <verse eid="ACT 10:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 10:19"/>And of Peter thinking over the vision, the Spirit said to him, “Behold, three men are seeking you.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> ECM, NA, and TR; NE and WH </char><char style="fq" closed="false">two men are seeking you</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; SBL, BYZ, and Tischendorf </char><char style="fq" closed="false">men are seeking you</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 10:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 10:20"/>But having risen, go down and proceed with them, doubting nothing, because I have sent them.” <verse eid="ACT 10:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 10:21"/>And Peter, having gone down to the men,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.21 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the men sent to him by Cornelius</char></note> said, “Behold, I am whom you⁺ seek; what <char style="add">is</char> the cause for which you⁺ are here?” <verse eid="ACT 10:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 10:22"/>And they said, “Cornelius, a centurion, a man righteous and fearing God—and being well testified to by all the nation of the Jews—was divinely instructed by a holy angel<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> F35 </char><char style="fq" closed="false">by an angel</char></note> to send for you to his house and to hear a message from you.” <verse eid="ACT 10:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 10:23"/>Therefore, having called them in, he lodged <char style="add">them</char>. And on the next day, having risen up,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.23 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR do not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">having risen up</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> he went out with them, and some of the brothers from Joppa went with him. <verse eid="ACT 10:23"/></para>

<para style="s">Peter Visits Cornelius</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 10:24"/>And on the next day, he entered<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.24 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">they entered</char></note> into Caesarea. Now Cornelius was expecting them, having called together his relatives and close friends. <verse eid="ACT 10:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 10:25"/>And as Peter was entering, Cornelius, having met him, having fallen at <char style="add">his</char> feet, worshiped <char style="add">him</char>. <verse eid="ACT 10:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 10:26"/>But Peter lifted him up, saying, “Rise up, I myself am also a man.” <verse eid="ACT 10:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 10:27"/>And talking with him, he entered, and he finds many having gathered together. <verse eid="ACT 10:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 10:28"/>And he was saying to them, “You⁺ know how it is unlawful for a man, a Jew, to unite himself or to come near to a foreigner. But God showed to me not to call a man common or unclean. <verse eid="ACT 10:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 10:29"/>Therefore also without objection I came, having been summoned. I ask, therefore for what reason did you⁺ summon me?” <verse eid="ACT 10:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 10:30"/>And Cornelius was saying, “Four days ago until this hour, the ninth hour, I was praying in my house;<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.30 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Four days ago, until this hour, I was fasting, and at the ninth hour I was praying in my house</char></note> and behold, a man in bright apparel stood before me, <verse eid="ACT 10:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 10:31"/>and he said, ‘Cornelius, your prayer was heard, and your alms have been remembered before God. <verse eid="ACT 10:31"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 10:32"/>Therefore send to Joppa and call for Simon, who is called Peter; he lodges in the house of Simon, a tanner by the sea.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.32 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">He will speak to you when he arrives</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note>’ <verse eid="ACT 10:32"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 10:33"/>Therefore I sent to you at once, and you did well, having come. Now, therefore, we are all present before God to hear all the things having been commanded you by the Lord.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.33 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">you by God</char></note>” <verse eid="ACT 10:33"/></para>

<para style="s">Good News for the Gentiles</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 10:34"/>And Peter, having opened the mouth, said, “Of a truth I understand that God is not One who shows partiality, <verse eid="ACT 10:34"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 10:35"/>but in every nation the one fearing Him and working righteousness is acceptable to Him, <verse eid="ACT 10:35"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 10:36"/>the word that He sent to the sons of Israel, proclaiming the gospel, peace by Jesus Christ—this One is Lord of all. <verse eid="ACT 10:36"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 10:37"/>You⁺ yourselves know the declaration having come through all Judea, having begun from Galilee, after the baptism that John proclaimed: <verse eid="ACT 10:37"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 10:38"/>Jesus from Nazareth—how God anointed Him with the Holy Spirit and with power—who went about doing good and healing all those being oppressed by the devil, because God was with Him. <verse eid="ACT 10:38"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="ACT 10:39"/>And we <char style="add">are</char> witnesses of all that He did—both in the region of the Jews and in Jerusalem—whom they also put to death, having hanged <char style="add">Him</char> on a tree. <verse eid="ACT 10:39"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="ACT 10:40"/>This One God raised up on the third day and gave Him to become manifest, <verse eid="ACT 10:40"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="ACT 10:41"/>not to all the people, but to the witnesses having been chosen beforehand by God, to us who ate and drank with Him after His rising out from the dead. <verse eid="ACT 10:41"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="ACT 10:42"/>And He instructed us to proclaim to the people and to testify fully that He is the One having been appointed by God <char style="add">as</char> Judge of the living and the dead. <verse eid="ACT 10:42"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="ACT 10:43"/>To this One all the prophets testify <char style="add">that</char> everyone believing in Him receives forgiveness of sins through His name.” <verse eid="ACT 10:43"/></para>

<para style="s">The Gentiles Receive the Holy SpiritActs 19:1–7</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="44" style="v" sid="ACT 10:44"/>Peter still speaking these words, the Holy Spirit fell upon all those hearing the word. <verse eid="ACT 10:44"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="45" style="v" sid="ACT 10:45"/>And the believers from the circumcision, as many as had come with Peter, were amazed that the gift of the Holy Spirit has been poured out even on the Gentiles. <verse eid="ACT 10:45"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="46" style="v" sid="ACT 10:46"/>For they were hearing them speaking in tongues and magnifying God. Then Peter answered, <verse eid="ACT 10:46"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="47" style="v" sid="ACT 10:47"/>“Is anyone able to withhold the water to baptize these who have received the Holy Spirit just as we also <char style="add">have</char>?” <verse eid="ACT 10:47"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="48" style="v" sid="ACT 10:48"/>And he commanded them to be baptized in the name of Jesus Christ.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">10.48 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> F35 </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of the Lord Jesus</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; RP and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of the Lord</char></note> Then they asked him to remain some days. <verse eid="ACT 10:48"/></para>

<chapter eid="ACT 10"/>

<chapter number="11" style="c" sid="ACT 11"/>

<para style="s">Peter’s Report at Jerusalem</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 11:1"/>Now the apostles and the brothers being in Judea heard that the Gentiles also had received the word of God. <verse eid="ACT 11:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 11:2"/>And when Peter went up to Jerusalem, those of the circumcision<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the circumcised believers</char></note> began contending with him, <verse eid="ACT 11:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 11:3"/>saying, “You went to men having uncircumcision and ate with them.” <verse eid="ACT 11:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 11:4"/>Now Peter, having begun, set <char style="add">it</char> forth to them in order, saying, <verse eid="ACT 11:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 11:5"/>“I was in the city of Joppa praying, and in a trance I saw a vision, a certain vessel like a great sheet descending, being let down out of heaven by four corners, and it came as far as me. <verse eid="ACT 11:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 11:6"/>Having looked intently on it, I was observing <char style="add">it</char>, and I saw the quadrupeds of the earth and the wild beasts and the creeping things and the birds of the air. <verse eid="ACT 11:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 11:7"/>And also I heard a voice saying to me, <char style="wj">‘Having risen up, Peter, kill and eat.’</char> <verse eid="ACT 11:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 11:8"/>But I said, ‘In no way, Lord, for never has a common<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">an impure</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; similarly in verse 9</char></note> or unclean <char style="add">thing</char> entered into my mouth.’ <verse eid="ACT 11:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 11:9"/>But for a second <char style="add">time</char> the voice answered<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">answered me</char></note> out of heaven, <char style="wj">‘What God has cleansed, you do not call common.’</char> <verse eid="ACT 11:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 11:10"/>Now this happened three times, and all was drawn up into heaven again. <verse eid="ACT 11:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 11:11"/>And behold, immediately three men having been sent to me from Caesarea stood at the house in which we were. <verse eid="ACT 11:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 11:12"/>And the Spirit told me to go with them, not having doubted. And these six brothers also went with me, and we entered into the man’s house, <verse eid="ACT 11:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 11:13"/>and he related to us how he saw the angel having stood in his house and having said, ‘Send forth<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> RP and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Send forth men</char></note> to Joppa and send for Simon who is called Peter, <verse eid="ACT 11:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 11:14"/>who will speak words to you by which you will be saved—you and all your household.’ <verse eid="ACT 11:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 11:15"/>And in my beginning to speak, the Holy Spirit fell upon them, even as also upon us in the beginning. <verse eid="ACT 11:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 11:16"/>And I remembered the word of the Lord, how He used to say, <char style="wj">‘John indeed baptized with water, but you⁺ will be baptized with the Holy Spirit.’</char> <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">‘John indeed baptized in water, but you will be baptized in the Holy Spirit.’</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; Acts 1:5</char></note><verse eid="ACT 11:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 11:17"/>If, then, God gave to them the same gift as also to us having believed on the Lord Jesus Christ,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> F35 </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Lord Jesus</char></note> how was I able to forbid God?” <verse eid="ACT 11:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 11:18"/>And having heard these things, they were silent and glorified God, saying, “Then indeed God has given also to the Gentiles repentance unto life.” <verse eid="ACT 11:18"/></para>

<para style="s">The Church at Antioch</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 11:19"/>Therefore, indeed, those having been scattered by the tribulation having taken place over Stephen passed through to Phoenicia and Cyprus and Antioch, speaking the word to no one except to Jews only. <verse eid="ACT 11:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 11:20"/>But some of them were men of Cyprus and Cyrene, who, having come into Antioch, were speaking also to the Hellenists,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Greeks</char></note> proclaiming the gospel—the Lord Jesus. <verse eid="ACT 11:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 11:21"/>And the hand of the Lord was with them, and a great number, having believed, turned to the Lord. <verse eid="ACT 11:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 11:22"/>Now the report was heard in the ears of the church being in Jerusalem concerning them, and they sent forth Barnabas to go as far as Antioch— <verse eid="ACT 11:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 11:23"/>who, having come and having seen the grace of God, rejoiced and was exhorting all to abide in the Lord with resolute purpose of heart. <verse eid="ACT 11:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 11:24"/>For he was a good man, and full of the Holy Spirit and of faith. And a great multitude was added to the Lord. <verse eid="ACT 11:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 11:25"/>And he went out to Tarsus to seek Saul, <verse eid="ACT 11:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 11:26"/>and having found <char style="add">him</char>, he brought <char style="add">him</char> to Antioch. And it came to pass <char style="add">that</char> they also gathered together a whole year in the church and taught a great multitude. And in Antioch the disciples were first called Christians. <verse eid="ACT 11:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 11:27"/>Now in these days, prophets came down from Jerusalem to Antioch. <verse eid="ACT 11:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 11:28"/>And one of them named Agabus, having risen up, signified by the Spirit <char style="add">that</char> a great famine is about to be over the whole world—<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.28 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the entire Roman world</char></note> which came to pass under Claudius.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">11.28 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Claudius Caesar</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 11:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 11:29"/>And the disciples, as anyone was prospered, each of them determined to send for ministry to the brothers dwelling in Judea, <verse eid="ACT 11:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 11:30"/>which also they did, having sent <char style="add">it</char> to the elders by the hand of Barnabas and Saul. <verse eid="ACT 11:30"/></para>

<chapter eid="ACT 11"/>

<chapter number="12" style="c" sid="ACT 12"/>

<para style="s">James Killed, Peter Imprisoned</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 12:1"/>Now at that time, Herod the king<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, King Herod Agrippa</char></note> put forth the hands to mistreat<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">reached out to harm</char></note> some of those of the church. <verse eid="ACT 12:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 12:2"/>And he put to death James the brother of John with the sword. <verse eid="ACT 12:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 12:3"/>And having seen that it is pleasing to the Jews, he proceeded to seize Peter also—now these were the days of the Unleavened—<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">seize Peter during the Feast of Unleavened Bread</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see Exodus 12:14–20.</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 12:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 12:4"/>whom also having arrested, he put in prison, having delivered <char style="add">him</char> to four sets of four soldiers to guard him, intending to bring him out to the people after the Passover. <verse eid="ACT 12:4"/></para>

<para style="s">The Rescue of Peter</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 12:5"/>Therefore indeed Peter was kept in the prison, but prayer was fervently<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">earnestly</char></note> being made to God by the church concerning him. <verse eid="ACT 12:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 12:6"/>And when Herod was about to bring him forth, on that night Peter was sleeping between two soldiers, having been bound with two chains, and guards before the door were keeping the prison. <verse eid="ACT 12:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 12:7"/>And behold, an angel of the Lord stood by, and a light shone in the cell. And having struck Peter’s side, he woke him up, saying, “Rise up in haste.” And his chains fell off the hands. <verse eid="ACT 12:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 12:8"/>And the angel said to him, “Gird yourself and put on your sandals.” And he did so. And he says to him, “Wrap around <char style="add">you</char> your cloak and follow me.” <verse eid="ACT 12:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 12:9"/>And having gone out, he was following, and he did not know that what is happening by means of the angel is real, but he was thinking he saw a vision. <verse eid="ACT 12:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 12:10"/>And having passed through a first and a second guard, they came to the iron gate leading into the city, which opened to them by itself. And having gone out, they went on through one street, and immediately the angel departed from him. <verse eid="ACT 12:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 12:11"/>And having come to himself, Peter said, “Now I know truly that the Lord sent forth His angel and delivered me out of the hand of Herod and of all the expectation of the people of the Jews.” <verse eid="ACT 12:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 12:12"/>And having considered, he came to the house of Mary the mother of John who is called Mark, where there were many gathered together and praying. <verse eid="ACT 12:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 12:13"/>And of him<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Peter</char></note> having knocked <char style="add">at</char> the door of the gate, a girl named Rhoda came to answer. <verse eid="ACT 12:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 12:14"/>And having recognized Peter’s voice, from joy she did not open the gate, but having run in, she reported Peter to be standing before the gate. <verse eid="ACT 12:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 12:15"/>And they said to her, “You are out of your mind.” But she kept insisting <char style="add">it</char> to be so. And they kept saying, “It is his angel.” <verse eid="ACT 12:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 12:16"/>But Peter continued knocking. And having opened, they saw him and were amazed. <verse eid="ACT 12:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 12:17"/>And having motioned to them with the hand to be silent, he related to them how the Lord had brought him out of the prison. And he said, “Report these things to James and to the brothers.” And having gone out, he went to another place. <verse eid="ACT 12:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 12:18"/>Now day having come, there was no small disturbance among the soldiers <char style="add">as to</char> what then was become of Peter. <verse eid="ACT 12:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 12:19"/>And Herod, having sought after him and not having found <char style="add">him</char>, having examined the guards, commanded <char style="add">them</char> to be led away. And having gone down from Judea to Caesarea, he stayed <char style="add">there</char>. <verse eid="ACT 12:19"/></para>

<para style="s">The Death of Herod</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 12:20"/>Now he was furiously angry<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">was in a furious dispute</char></note> with the Tyrians and Sidonians, and they came to him with one accord. And having gained Blastus, who <char style="add">was</char> over the bedchamber of the king, they were seeking peace because of their region being nourished by the king’s. <verse eid="ACT 12:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 12:21"/>Now on the appointed day Herod, having put on royal apparel and having sat on the throne, was making an address to them. <verse eid="ACT 12:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 12:22"/>And the people were crying out, “The voice of a god and not of a man!” <verse eid="ACT 12:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 12:23"/>And immediately an angel of the Lord struck him because he did not give the glory to God. And having been eaten by worms, he breathed his last. <verse eid="ACT 12:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 12:24"/>But the word of God<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.24 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> WH </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Lord</char></note> continued to grow and to multiply. <verse eid="ACT 12:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 12:25"/>And Barnabas and Saul returned, having fulfilled the ministry to Jerusalem,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">12.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">returned, having fulfilled the ministry, to Jerusalem</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; NE and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">returned, having fulfilled the ministry, from Jerusalem</char></note> having taken with <char style="add">them</char> John, the one having been called Mark. <verse eid="ACT 12:25"/></para>

<chapter eid="ACT 12"/>

<chapter number="13" style="c" sid="ACT 13"/>

<para style="s">Paul’s First Missionary Journey Begins</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 13:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Acts 18:23–28</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Acts 15:36–41</char></note>Now there were<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">certain</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> prophets and teachers in Antioch being <char style="add">there</char> in the church: Both Barnabas and Simeon who was called Niger, and Lucius the Cyrenian, and Manaen brought up with Herod the tetrarch, and Saul. <verse eid="ACT 13:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 13:2"/>Now <char style="add">in</char> their ministering to the Lord and fasting, the Holy Spirit said, “Now set apart unto Me Barnabas and Saul for the work to which I have summoned them.” <verse eid="ACT 13:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 13:3"/>Then, having fasted and having prayed and having laid the hands on them, they sent <char style="add">them</char> off. <verse eid="ACT 13:3"/></para>

<para style="s">On Cyprus</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 13:4"/>Indeed, therefore, having been sent forth by the Holy Spirit, they went down to Seleucia, and they sailed from there to Cyprus. <verse eid="ACT 13:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 13:5"/>And having come into Salamis, they began proclaiming the word of God in the synagogues of the Jews. And they also had John <char style="add">as</char> a helper. <verse eid="ACT 13:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 13:6"/>Now having passed through the whole island<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">through the island</char></note> as far as Paphos, they found a man—a certain a magician, a Jewish false prophet—whose name <char style="add">was</char> Bar-Jesus, <verse eid="ACT 13:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 13:7"/>who was with the proconsul, Sergius Paulus, an intelligent man. This <char style="add">man</char>, having summoned Barnabas and Saul, desired to hear the word of God. <verse eid="ACT 13:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 13:8"/>But Elymas the magician (for his name is translated thus) was opposing them, seeking to turn away the proconsul from the faith. <verse eid="ACT 13:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 13:9"/>And Saul, the one also <char style="add">called</char> Paul, having been filled with the Holy Spirit, having looked intently upon him, <verse eid="ACT 13:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 13:10"/>said, “O full of all deceit and all craftiness, son of the devil, enemy of all righteousness, will you not cease perverting the straight ways of the Lord? <verse eid="ACT 13:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 13:11"/>And now behold, the hand of the Lord <char style="add">is</char> upon you, and you will be blind, not seeing the sun for a season.” And immediately mist and darkness fell upon him, and going about, he was seeking someone to lead <char style="add">him</char> by the hand. <verse eid="ACT 13:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 13:12"/>Then the proconsul, having seen that having happened, believed, being astonished at the teaching of the Lord. <verse eid="ACT 13:12"/></para>

<para style="s">In Pisidian Antioch</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 13:13"/>And those around Paul, having sailed from Paphos, came to Perga of Pamphylia. But John, having departed from them, returned to Jerusalem. <verse eid="ACT 13:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 13:14"/>Now having passed through from Perga, they came to Antioch of Pisidia, and having gone into the synagogue on the day of the Sabbaths, they sat down. <verse eid="ACT 13:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 13:15"/>And after the reading of the Law and of the Prophets, the synagogue rulers sent to them, saying, “Men, brothers, if there is any word of exhortation among you⁺ toward the people, speak.” <verse eid="ACT 13:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 13:16"/>And Paul, having risen up and having motioned with the hand, said, “Men, Israelites, and those fearing God, listen: <verse eid="ACT 13:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 13:17"/>The God of this people Israel<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ </char><char style="fq" closed="false">The God of the people</char></note> chose our fathers and exalted the people in the sojourn in the land of Egypt, and with uplifted arm He brought them out of it, <verse eid="ACT 13:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 13:18"/>and for a period of about forty years He endured their ways in the wilderness,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.18 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">desert</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 13:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 13:19"/>and having destroyed seven nations in the land of Canaan, He gave as an inheritance their land— <verse eid="ACT 13:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 13:20"/>in about four hundred and fifty years. And after these things, He gave <char style="add">them</char> judges until Samuel the prophet. <verse eid="ACT 13:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 13:21"/>Then they asked for a king, and God gave to them Saul son of Kish, a man of the tribe of Benjamin, forty years. <verse eid="ACT 13:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 13:22"/>And having removed him, He raised up David to them as king, to whom He also said, having testified: ‘I have found David the <char style="add">son</char> of Jesse a man according to My heart, who will do all My will.’ <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> See 1 Samuel 13:14.</char></note><verse eid="ACT 13:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 13:23"/>Of the seed of this <char style="add">man</char>, according to promise, God brought to Israel a Savior, Jesus—<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.23 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> RP </char><char style="fq" closed="false">brought salvation to Israel</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 13:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 13:24"/>John having proclaimed before the face of His coming a baptism of repentance to all the people of Israel.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.24 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to Israel</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 13:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 13:25"/>And as John was fulfilling the course, he was saying, ‘Whom do you⁺ suppose me to be? I am not <char style="add">He</char>, but behold, He comes after me of whom I am not worthy to untie a sandal of the feet.’ <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Luke 3:16; see also Matthew 3:11, Mark 1:7, and John 1:27.</char></note><verse eid="ACT 13:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 13:26"/>Men, brothers, sons of the family of Abraham, and those among you⁺ fearing God, to us<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.26 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to you</char></note> the message of this salvation was sent forth. <verse eid="ACT 13:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 13:27"/>For those dwelling in Jerusalem and their rulers, not having known Him and the voices of the prophets that are being read on every Sabbath, having condemned <char style="add">Him</char>, they fulfilled <char style="add">them</char>. <verse eid="ACT 13:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 13:28"/>And having found no cause of death, they begged Pilate to put Him to death. <verse eid="ACT 13:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 13:29"/>And when they finished all the things having been written about Him, having taken <char style="add">Him</char> down from the tree, they put <char style="add">Him</char> in a tomb. <verse eid="ACT 13:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 13:30"/>But God raised Him out from the dead, <verse eid="ACT 13:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 13:31"/>who appeared for many days to those having come up with Him from Galilee to Jerusalem, who are now<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.31 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR do not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">now</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> His witnesses to the people. <verse eid="ACT 13:31"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 13:32"/>And we preach the gospel to you⁺, the promise having been made to the fathers, <verse eid="ACT 13:32"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 13:33"/>that God has fulfilled this to us their children, having raised up Jesus, as it has also been written in the second psalm: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="ACT 13:33">‘You are My Son; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 13:33">today I have begotten You.’ <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.33 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Psalm 2:7; or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">today I have become Your Father</char></note><verse eid="ACT 13:33"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 13:34"/>And that He raised Him out from the dead, no more being about to return to decay, He spoke thus: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="ACT 13:34">‘I will give to you⁺ the holy <char style="add">blessings</char>, the faithful ones, of David.’ <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.34 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">I will give you the holy and sure blessings promised to David</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; Isaiah 55:3</char></note><verse eid="ACT 13:34"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 13:35"/>So also, He says in another <char style="add">place</char>: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="ACT 13:35">‘You will not allow Your Holy One to see decay.’ <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.35 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Psalm 16:10</char></note><verse eid="ACT 13:35"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 13:36"/>For indeed David, having served the purpose of God in his own generation, fell asleep and was added to his fathers, and he saw decay. <verse eid="ACT 13:36"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 13:37"/>But the One God raised up did not see decay. <verse eid="ACT 13:37"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 13:38"/>Therefore be it known to you⁺, men, brothers, that through this One forgiveness of sins is proclaimed to you⁺. <verse eid="ACT 13:38"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="ACT 13:39"/>And in Him everyone believing is justified from all things from which you⁺ were not able to be justified in the law of Moses. <verse eid="ACT 13:39"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="ACT 13:40"/>Take heed, therefore, lest that having been said in the prophets might come about:<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.40 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to you</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 13:40"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="ACT 13:41"/>‘Behold, scoffers, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 13:41">and wonder and perish; </para>

<para style="q1" vid="ACT 13:41">for I am working a work in your⁺ days, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 13:41">a work that you⁺ would never believe, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 13:41">even if one should declare it to you⁺.’” <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.41 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Habakkuk 1:5 (see also LXX)</char></note><verse eid="ACT 13:41"/></para>

<para style="s">A Light for the GentilesIsaiah 49:1–6</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="ACT 13:42"/>And <char style="add">on</char> their having departed, they were begging<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.42 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">And having gone forth out of the synagogue of the Jews, the Gentiles were begging</char></note> these words to be spoken to them on the next Sabbath. <verse eid="ACT 13:42"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="ACT 13:43"/>And the synagogue having been dismissed, many of the Jews and worshiping converts followed Paul and Barnabas, who, speaking to them, kept persuading them to continue in the grace of God. <verse eid="ACT 13:43"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="44" style="v" sid="ACT 13:44"/>And on the coming Sabbath, almost all the city was gathered together to hear the word of the Lord.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.44 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">word of God</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 13:44"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="45" style="v" sid="ACT 13:45"/>But the Jews, having seen the crowds, were filled with jealousy, and they began contradicting<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.45 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">contradicting and opposing</char></note> the things spoken by Paul, blaspheming. <verse eid="ACT 13:45"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="46" style="v" sid="ACT 13:46"/>And Paul and Barnabas, having spoken boldly, said, “It was necessary <char style="add">for</char> the word of God to be spoken first to you⁺. But since you⁺ thrust it away and do not judge yourselves worthy of eternal life, behold, we are turning to the Gentiles. <verse eid="ACT 13:46"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="47" style="v" sid="ACT 13:47"/>For thus the Lord has commanded us: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="ACT 13:47">‘I have placed you as a light for the Gentiles, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 13:47"><char style="add">that</char> you may be for salvation to the end of the earth.’”<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.47 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">nations</char></note> <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">13.47 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Isaiah 49:6</char></note><verse eid="ACT 13:47"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="48" style="v" sid="ACT 13:48"/>And the Gentiles hearing were rejoicing and glorifying the word of the Lord, and as many as were appointed to eternal life believed. <verse eid="ACT 13:48"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="49" style="v" sid="ACT 13:49"/>And the word of the Lord was carried through the whole region. <verse eid="ACT 13:49"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="50" style="v" sid="ACT 13:50"/>But the Jews incited the worshiping women of honorable position and the principals of the city, and they stirred up a persecution against Paul and Barnabas and expelled them from their district. <verse eid="ACT 13:50"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="51" style="v" sid="ACT 13:51"/>And having shaken off the dust of the feet against them, they went to Iconium. <verse eid="ACT 13:51"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="52" style="v" sid="ACT 13:52"/>And the disciples were filled with joy and the Holy Spirit. <verse eid="ACT 13:52"/></para>

<chapter eid="ACT 13"/>

<chapter number="14" style="c" sid="ACT 14"/>

<para style="s">Paul and Barnabas at Iconium</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 14:1"/>Now it came to pass in Iconium, according to the same, <char style="add">that</char> they entered into the synagogue of the Jews and spoke so that a large number of both Jews and Greeks believed. <verse eid="ACT 14:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 14:2"/>But the unbelieving Jews stirred up and poisoned the minds of the Gentiles against the brothers. <verse eid="ACT 14:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 14:3"/>Therefore indeed they stayed a long time, speaking boldly for the Lord, testifying to the word of His grace, granting signs and wonders to be done through their hands. <verse eid="ACT 14:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 14:4"/>Now the multitude of the city was divided, and indeed some were with the Jews, but some with the apostles. <verse eid="ACT 14:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 14:5"/>And when there was a rush of both the Gentiles and Jews, with their rulers, to mistreat and to stone them, <verse eid="ACT 14:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 14:6"/>having become aware, they fled to the Lycaonian cities Lystra and Derbe, and the surrounding region, <verse eid="ACT 14:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 14:7"/>and there they continued preaching the gospel. <verse eid="ACT 14:7"/></para>

<para style="s">The Visit to Lystra and Derbe</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 14:8"/>And in Lystra a certain man was sitting, crippled in the feet, lame from the womb of his mother, who had never walked. <verse eid="ACT 14:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 14:9"/>This <char style="add">man</char> heard Paul speaking, who, having looked intently at him and having seen that he has faith to be healed, <verse eid="ACT 14:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 14:10"/>said in a loud voice, “Stand upright on your feet!” And he sprang up and began to walk. <verse eid="ACT 14:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 14:11"/>And the crowds, having seen what Paul had done, lifted up their voice in Lycaonian, saying, “The gods have come down to us, having become like men!” <verse eid="ACT 14:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 14:12"/>And Barnabas they began calling Zeus; and Paul, Hermes, because he was the leading speaker. <verse eid="ACT 14:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 14:13"/>And the priest of Zeus, being just outside the city, having brought oxen and wreaths to the gates, was desiring with the crowds to sacrifice. <verse eid="ACT 14:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 14:14"/>But the apostles Barnabas and Paul, having heard, having torn their garments, rushed out into the crowd, crying out <verse eid="ACT 14:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 14:15"/>and saying, “Men, why do you⁺ do these things? We also are men of like nature with you⁺, proclaiming the gospel to you⁺ to turn from these vain <char style="add">things</char> to the living God, who made the heaven and the earth and the sea and all the things in them, <verse eid="ACT 14:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 14:16"/>who in the generations past allowed all the nations to go their ways. <verse eid="ACT 14:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 14:17"/>And yet He did not leave Himself without witness, doing good, giving to you⁺ rains from heaven and fruitful seasons, filling your⁺ hearts with food and gladness.” <verse eid="ACT 14:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 14:18"/>Even saying these things, they hardly stopped the crowds from sacrificing to them. <verse eid="ACT 14:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 14:19"/>But Jews came from Antioch and Iconium, and having persuaded the crowds, and having stoned Paul, they dragged <char style="add">him</char> outside the city, supposing him to have died. <verse eid="ACT 14:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 14:20"/>But the disciples having surrounded him, having risen up, he entered into the city. And on the next day he went out with Barnabas to Derbe. <verse eid="ACT 14:20"/></para>

<para style="s">Strengthening the Disciples</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 14:21"/>And having proclaimed the gospel to that city and having discipled many, they returned to Lystra and to Iconium and to Antioch, <verse eid="ACT 14:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 14:22"/>strengthening the souls of the disciples, exhorting <char style="add">them</char> to continue in the faith and that “through many tribulations it is necessary for us to enter into the kingdom of God.” <verse eid="ACT 14:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 14:23"/>And having appointed elders for them in every church, having prayed, with fasting they committed them to the Lord, in whom they had believed. <verse eid="ACT 14:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 14:24"/>And having passed through Pisidia, they came to Pamphylia, <verse eid="ACT 14:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 14:25"/>and having spoken the word in Perga, they went down to Attalia. <verse eid="ACT 14:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 14:26"/>And from there they sailed to Antioch, from where they had been committed to the grace of God for the work that they had fulfilled. <verse eid="ACT 14:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 14:27"/>And having arrived and having gathered together the church, they began declaring all that God had done with them, and that He had opened a door of faith to the Gentiles. <verse eid="ACT 14:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 14:28"/>And they remained no little time with the disciples. </para>

<para style="p" vid="ACT 14:28"> BYZ and TR <char style="add">their city</char> TR <char style="add">to us</char> BYZ and TR <char style="add">our</char> BYZ and TR include <char style="add">there</char>.<verse eid="ACT 14:28"/></para>

<chapter eid="ACT 14"/>

<chapter number="15" style="c" sid="ACT 15"/>

<para style="s">The Dispute over Circumcision</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 15:1"/>But certain ones having come down from Judea were teaching the brothers, “Unless you⁺ are circumcised according to the custom of Moses, you⁺ are not able to be saved.” <verse eid="ACT 15:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 15:2"/>There having been, then, no small commotion and discussion by Paul and Barnabas with them, they appointed Paul and Barnabas and certain others out of them to go up to Jerusalem, to the apostles and elders, about this question. <verse eid="ACT 15:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 15:3"/>Therefore indeed, having been sent forward by the church, they were passing through both<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR do not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">both</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> Phoenicia and Samaria, relating in detail the conversion of the Gentiles, and they were bringing great joy to all the brothers. <verse eid="ACT 15:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 15:4"/>And having come to Jerusalem, they were welcomed by the church and the apostles and the elders. And they declared all that God had done with them.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> GOC includes </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and how He had opened a door of faith to the Gentiles</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 15:4"/></para>

<para style="s">The Council at JerusalemAmos 9:11–15</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 15:5"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Galatians 2:1–10</char></note>Now certain ones of those who believed from the sect of the Pharisees rose up, saying, “It is necessary to circumcise them, and to command <char style="add">them</char> to keep the law of Moses.” <verse eid="ACT 15:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 15:6"/>And the apostles and the elders were gathered together to see about this matter. <verse eid="ACT 15:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 15:7"/>And much discussion having taken place, Peter having risen up, said to them, “Men, brothers, you⁺ know that from early days God chose among you⁺<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">us</char></note> <char style="add">for</char> the Gentiles to hear by my mouth the word of the gospel, and to believe. <verse eid="ACT 15:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 15:8"/>And the heart-knowing God testified to them, having given <char style="add">them</char> the Holy Spirit, as also to us. <verse eid="ACT 15:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 15:9"/>And He made no distinction between both us and them, having purified their hearts by faith. <verse eid="ACT 15:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 15:10"/>Now, therefore, why are you⁺ testing God, putting upon the neck of the disciples a yoke that neither our fathers nor we have been able to bear? <verse eid="ACT 15:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 15:11"/>But we believe to be saved through the grace of the Lord Jesus,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Lord Jesus Christ</char></note> in the same manner <char style="add">as</char> they also.” <verse eid="ACT 15:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 15:12"/>Now the whole multitude kept silent and were listening to Barnabas and Paul relating what signs and wonders God had done among the Gentiles by them. <verse eid="ACT 15:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 15:13"/>And after they were silent, James answered, saying, “Men, brothers, hear me. <verse eid="ACT 15:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 15:14"/>Simeon<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Simon</char><char style="ft" closed="false">, a variant of Simeon</char></note> related how God first visited to take out of the Gentiles a people for His name. <verse eid="ACT 15:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 15:15"/>And the words of the prophets agree with this, as it is written: <verse eid="ACT 15:15"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 15:16"/>‘After these things I will return, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 15:16">and I will rebuild the tabernacle of David that has fallen, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="ACT 15:16">and its ruins I will rebuild, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 15:16">and I will set it upright, <verse eid="ACT 15:16"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 15:17"/>so that the remnant of men may seek out the Lord, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 15:17">and all the Gentiles, upon whom has been called My name—upon them, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="ACT 15:17">says the Lord, doing these things <verse eid="ACT 15:17"/></para>

<para style="q2"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 15:18"/>known from the age.’ <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.18 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Amos 9:11–12 (see also LXX); BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">says the Lord, who does all these things. </char><char style="fq" closed="false">18</char><char style="fq" closed="false">Known unto God are all His works from the age.</char></note><verse eid="ACT 15:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 15:19"/>Therefore I judge not to trouble those from the Gentiles turning to God, <verse eid="ACT 15:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 15:20"/>but to write to them to abstain from the pollutions of idols, and <char style="add">from</char> sexual immorality, and <char style="add">from</char> that which is strangled, and from blood. <verse eid="ACT 15:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 15:21"/>For Moses has ones proclaiming him in every city from generations of old, being read in the synagogues on every Sabbath.” <verse eid="ACT 15:21"/></para>

<para style="s">The Letter to the Gentile Believers</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 15:22"/>Then it seemed good to the apostles and to the elders, with the whole church, having chosen out of them to send men to Antioch with Paul and Barnabas: Judas called Barsabbas<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> ALT, F35, and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Barsabas</char></note> and Silas, leading men among the brothers, <verse eid="ACT 15:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 15:23"/>having written by their hand: </para>

<para style="p" vid="ACT 15:23">The apostles and the elders, brothers, </para>

<para style="p" vid="ACT 15:23">To those brothers among the Gentiles in Antioch and Syria and Cilicia: </para>

<para style="p" vid="ACT 15:23">Greetings. <verse eid="ACT 15:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 15:24"/>Inasmuch as we have heard that some went out from us, to whom we gave no instructions, <char style="add">and that</char> they troubled you⁺ by words, upsetting your⁺ minds,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.24 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">by saying that you must be circumcised and keep the law</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 15:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 15:25"/>it seemed good to us, having come with one accord, having chosen men to send to you⁺ with our beloved Barnabas and Paul, <verse eid="ACT 15:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 15:26"/>men having handed over their lives for the name of our Lord Jesus Christ. <verse eid="ACT 15:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 15:27"/>Therefore we have sent Judas and Silas, and they are telling the same things by word. <verse eid="ACT 15:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 15:28"/>For it seemed good to the Holy Spirit and to us to lay upon you⁺ no further burden except these necessary things: <verse eid="ACT 15:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 15:29"/>to abstain from things sacrificed to idols, and from blood, and from what is strangled, and from sexual immorality. Keeping yourselves from these, you⁺ will do well. </para>

<para style="p" vid="ACT 15:29">Farewell. <verse eid="ACT 15:29"/></para>

<para style="s">The Believers at Antioch Rejoice</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 15:30"/>Indeed, therefore, having been sent off, they went to Antioch, and having gathered the multitude, they delivered the letter. <verse eid="ACT 15:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 15:31"/>And having read <char style="add">it</char>, they rejoiced at the encouragement. <verse eid="ACT 15:31"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 15:32"/>Both Judas and Silas, also being prophets themselves, exhorted and strengthened the brothers by much talk. <verse eid="ACT 15:32"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 15:33"/>And having continued a time, they were sent away in peace from the brothers to those having sent them.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.33 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to return to the apostles</char><char style="ft" closed="false">. TR includes </char><char style="fq" closed="false">34</char><char style="fq" closed="false">But it seemed good to Silas to remain there.</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 15:33"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 15:35"/>But Paul and Barnabas stayed in Antioch, teaching and preaching the good news—with many others also—the word of the Lord. <verse eid="ACT 15:35"/></para>

<para style="s">Paul’s Second Missionary Journey BeginsActs 13:1–3</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 15:36"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Acts 18:23–28</char></note>Now after some days, Paul said to Barnabas, “Indeed, having turned back, let us look after the brothers<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.36 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">our brothers</char></note> in every city in which we have proclaimed the word of the Lord—how they are.” <verse eid="ACT 15:36"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 15:37"/>Now Barnabas purposed also to take along John, called Mark. <verse eid="ACT 15:37"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 15:38"/>But Paul was thinking it fit not to take him along, the one having withdrawn from them from Pamphylia and not having gone with them to the work. <verse eid="ACT 15:38"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="ACT 15:39"/>Therefore a sharp disagreement arose, so that they separated from one another. And Barnabas, having taken Mark, sailed to Cyprus. <verse eid="ACT 15:39"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="ACT 15:40"/>But Paul, having chosen Silas, went out, having been committed to the grace of the Lord<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">15.40 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of God</char></note> by the brothers. <verse eid="ACT 15:40"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="ACT 15:41"/>And he was passing through Syria and Cilicia, strengthening the churches. <verse eid="ACT 15:41"/></para>

<chapter eid="ACT 15"/>

<chapter number="16" style="c" sid="ACT 16"/>

<para style="s">Timothy Joins Paul and Silas</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 16:1"/>And he came also to Derbe and to Lystra. And behold, a certain disciple was there, named Timothy, the son of a believing Jewish woman and a Greek father, <verse eid="ACT 16:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 16:2"/>who was well spoken of by the brothers in Lystra and Iconium. <verse eid="ACT 16:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 16:3"/>Paul wanted this one to go out with him, and having taken <char style="add">him</char>, he circumcised him on account of the Jews being in those parts; for they all knew that his father was a Greek. <verse eid="ACT 16:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 16:4"/>And while they were passing through the cities, they were delivering to them the decrees to keep—the ones decided on by the apostles and elders who <char style="add">were</char> in Jerusalem. <verse eid="ACT 16:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 16:5"/>So indeed the churches were strengthened in the faith and were increasing in number every day. <verse eid="ACT 16:5"/></para>

<para style="s">Paul’s Vision of the Macedonian</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 16:6"/>And having passed through Phrygia and the Galatian region, having been forbidden by the Holy Spirit to speak the word in Asia,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in the province of Asia</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; Asia was a Roman province in what is now western Turkey. </char></note> <verse eid="ACT 16:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 16:7"/>and having come down to Mysia, they were attempting to go into Bithynia, and the Spirit of Jesus<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Spirit</char></note> did not allow them. <verse eid="ACT 16:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 16:8"/>And having passed by Mysia, they came down to Troas. <verse eid="ACT 16:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 16:9"/>And a vision appeared to Paul during the night: A certain man of Macedonia was standing and beseeching him and saying, “Having passed over into Macedonia, help us.” <verse eid="ACT 16:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 16:10"/>And when he had seen the vision, immediately we sought to go out into Macedonia, concluding that God<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">that the Lord</char></note> had summoned us to preach the gospel to them. <verse eid="ACT 16:10"/></para>

<para style="s">Lydia’s Conversion in PhilippiRevelation 2:18–29</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 16:11"/>And having sailed<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">having sailed, therefore</char></note> from Troas, we made a straight course to Samothrace, and on the following day to Neapolis, <verse eid="ACT 16:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 16:12"/>and from there to Philippi, which is a leading city of the district of Macedonia—a colony.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to the Roman colony of Philippi, the leading city of that district of Macedonia</char></note> Now we were staying some days in this city. <verse eid="ACT 16:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 16:13"/>And on the day of the Sabbaths, we went outside the city gate,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the city</char></note> by a river, where <char style="add">there</char> was customary to be prayer. And having sat down, we began speaking to the women having gathered. <verse eid="ACT 16:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 16:14"/>And a certain woman named Lydia, a seller of purple of the city of Thyatira, worshiping God, was listening. The Lord opened her heart to attend to the things being spoken by Paul. <verse eid="ACT 16:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 16:15"/>And when she was baptized, and her house, she begged, saying, “If you⁺ have judged me to be faithful to the Lord, having entered into my house, abide.” And she persuaded us. <verse eid="ACT 16:15"/></para>

<para style="s">Paul and Silas Imprisoned</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 16:16"/>Now it happened <char style="add">in</char> our going to the prayer <char style="add">that</char> a certain girl having a spirit of Python<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">a spirit of divination</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; that is, a spirit of divination named after the mythical serpent slain by Apollo</char></note> met us, who was bringing her masters much gain by fortune-telling. <verse eid="ACT 16:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 16:17"/>Having followed Paul and us,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> GOC, ALT, and F35 </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Paul and Silas</char></note> she was crying out, saying, “These men are servants of the Most High God, who proclaim to you⁺<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to us</char></note> the way of salvation!” <verse eid="ACT 16:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 16:18"/>And she continued this for many days. And Paul, having been distressed and having turned, said to the spirit, “I command you in the name of Jesus Christ to come out from her!” And it came out the same hour. <verse eid="ACT 16:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 16:19"/>And her masters, having seen that their hope of profit was gone, having taken hold of Paul and Silas, dragged <char style="add">them</char> into the marketplace before the rulers. <verse eid="ACT 16:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 16:20"/>And having brought them up to the magistrates, they said, “These men, being Jews, exceedingly trouble our city <verse eid="ACT 16:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 16:21"/>and proclaim customs not lawful for us, being Romans, to accept nor to practice.” <verse eid="ACT 16:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 16:22"/>And the crowd rose up together against them, and the magistrates, having torn off their garments, were commanding that they be beaten with rods. <verse eid="ACT 16:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 16:23"/>And having laid many blows on them, they cast <char style="add">them</char> into prison, having charged the jailer to keep them securely, <verse eid="ACT 16:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 16:24"/>who, having received such an order, threw them into the inner prison and fastened their feet in the stocks. <verse eid="ACT 16:24"/></para>

<para style="s">The Conversion of the Jailer</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 16:25"/>Now toward midnight, Paul and Silas, praying, were singing praises to God. And the prisoners were listening to them. <verse eid="ACT 16:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 16:26"/>And suddenly there was a great earthquake, so that the foundations of the prison house were shaken, and immediately all the doors were opened, and the chains of all were loosed. <verse eid="ACT 16:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 16:27"/>And the jailer, having been awoken and having seen the doors of the prison open, having drawn his sword, was about to kill himself, supposing the prisoners to have escaped. <verse eid="ACT 16:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 16:28"/>But Paul called out in a loud voice, saying, “Do not harm yourself, for we are all here!” <verse eid="ACT 16:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 16:29"/>And having called for lights, he rushed in, and having become terrified, he fell down before Paul and Silas. <verse eid="ACT 16:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 16:30"/>And having brought them out, he was saying, “Sirs, what is necessary for me to do so that I may be saved?” <verse eid="ACT 16:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 16:31"/>And they said, “Believe on the Lord Jesus<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16.31 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Lord Jesus Christ</char></note> and you will be saved, you and your house.” <verse eid="ACT 16:31"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 16:32"/>And they spoke the word of the Lord<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">16.32 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> WH </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of God</char></note> to him, along with all those in his house. <verse eid="ACT 16:32"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 16:33"/>And having taken them in that hour of the night, he washed <char style="add">them</char> from the wounds, and immediately he was baptized, and all his <char style="add">own</char>. <verse eid="ACT 16:33"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 16:34"/>And having brought them into the house, he set a table and rejoiced with all <char style="add">his</char> household, having believed in God. <verse eid="ACT 16:34"/></para>

<para style="s">An Official Apology</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 16:35"/>And day having come, the magistrates sent the officers, saying, “Release those men.” <verse eid="ACT 16:35"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 16:36"/>And the jailer reported these words to Paul: “The captains have sent that you⁺ may be let go. Now, therefore, having gone out, depart in peace.” <verse eid="ACT 16:36"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 16:37"/>But Paul was saying to them, “Having beaten us publicly, uncondemned men being Romans, they cast <char style="add">us</char> into prison, and now do they throw us out secretly? No indeed! Rather, having come themselves, let them bring us out.” <verse eid="ACT 16:37"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 16:38"/>And the officers reported these words to the captains, and they were afraid, having heard that they are Romans. <verse eid="ACT 16:38"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="ACT 16:39"/>And having come, they appealed to them, and having brought <char style="add">them</char> out, they were asking <char style="add">them</char> to go out of the city. <verse eid="ACT 16:39"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="ACT 16:40"/>And having gone out of the prison, they came to Lydia, and having seen <char style="add">them</char>, they exhorted the brothers and went out. <verse eid="ACT 16:40"/></para>

<chapter eid="ACT 16"/>

<chapter number="17" style="c" sid="ACT 17"/>

<para style="s">The Uproar in Thessalonica</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 17:1"/>And having passed through Amphipolis and Apollonia, they came to Thessalonica, where there was a synagogue of the Jews. <verse eid="ACT 17:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 17:2"/>And according to the custom of Paul, he went in to them, and for three Sabbaths he reasoned with them from the Scriptures, <verse eid="ACT 17:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 17:3"/>opening and setting forth that it was necessary for the Christ to have suffered and to have risen out from the dead, and that “this Jesus whom I proclaim to you⁺ is the Christ.” <verse eid="ACT 17:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 17:4"/>And some of them were obedient and joined themselves to Paul and to Silas, along with a great multitude of the worshiping Greeks and not a few of the leading women. <verse eid="ACT 17:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 17:5"/>But the Jews, having become jealous and having taken along<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">17.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the unbelieving Jews, having taken along</char></note> certain wicked men of the market-loungers, and having collected a crowd, set the city in uproar. And having assailed the house of Jason, they were seeking them to bring out to the people. <verse eid="ACT 17:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 17:6"/>But not having found them, they dragged Jason and certain brothers before the city authorities, crying out, “These ones, having upset the world, have come here also, <verse eid="ACT 17:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 17:7"/>whom Jason has received. And these all do contrary to the decrees of Caesar, proclaiming another to be king—Jesus!” <verse eid="ACT 17:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 17:8"/>And they stirred up the crowd and the city authorities hearing these things. <verse eid="ACT 17:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 17:9"/>And having taken security from Jason and the rest, they let them go. <verse eid="ACT 17:9"/></para>

<para style="s">The Character of the Bereans</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 17:10"/>And the brothers sent away both Paul and Silas immediately by night to Berea, who, having arrived, went into the synagogue of the Jews. <verse eid="ACT 17:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 17:11"/>Now these, who were more noble than those in Thessalonica, received the word with all readiness, every day examining the Scriptures, if these things were so. <verse eid="ACT 17:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 17:12"/>Therefore many of them indeed believed, and not a few of the prominent Grecian women and men. <verse eid="ACT 17:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 17:13"/>But when the Jews from Thessalonica knew that the word of God also was proclaimed by Paul in Berea, they came there also, stirring up and agitating<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">17.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR do not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and agitating</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> the crowds. <verse eid="ACT 17:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 17:14"/>And then immediately the brothers sent away Paul to go as to the sea. And both Silas and Timothy remained there. <verse eid="ACT 17:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 17:15"/>And those escorting Paul brought <char style="add">him</char> unto Athens, and having received a command to Silas and Timothy that as quickly as possible they should come to him, they departed. <verse eid="ACT 17:15"/></para>

<para style="s">Paul in Athens</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 17:16"/>Now Paul in Athens waiting for them, his spirit was provoked in him, seeing the city to be utterly idolatrous. <verse eid="ACT 17:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 17:17"/>So indeed he was reasoning in the synagogue with the Jews and those worshiping, and in the marketplace on every day with those meeting. <verse eid="ACT 17:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 17:18"/>And also some of the Epicureans and Stoics, philosophers, encountered him, and some were saying, “What may this babbler desire to say?” but others, “He seems to be a proclaimer of strange gods,” because he was proclaiming the gospel—Jesus and the resurrection. <verse eid="ACT 17:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 17:19"/>And having taken hold of him, they brought <char style="add">him</char> to the Areopagus,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">17.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Ares Hill</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Mars Hill</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verse 22</char></note> saying, “Are we able to know what this new teaching <char style="add">is</char> that is spoken by you? <verse eid="ACT 17:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 17:20"/>For you are bringing some strange things to our ears. We resolve, therefore, to know what these things wish to be.” <verse eid="ACT 17:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 17:21"/>Now all the Athenians and the visiting foreigners spent their time on nothing other than to say something and to hear something new. <verse eid="ACT 17:21"/></para>

<para style="s">Paul’s Address in the Areopagus</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 17:22"/>And Paul, having stood in the midst<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">17.22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in the meeting</char></note> of the Areopagus, was saying, “Men, Athenians, in all things I perceive you⁺ as very religious. <verse eid="ACT 17:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 17:23"/>For passing through and examining your⁺ objects of worship, I even found an altar on which had been inscribed: </para>

<para style="p" vid="ACT 17:23">TO AN UNKNOWN GOD.</para>

<para style="p" vid="ACT 17:23">Therefore whom you⁺ worship without knowing, this I proclaim to you⁺. <verse eid="ACT 17:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 17:24"/>The God having made the world and all things that <char style="add">are</char> in it, He, being Lord of heaven and earth, does not dwell in hand-made temples, <verse eid="ACT 17:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 17:25"/>nor is He served by hands of men as needing anything—He <char style="add">who</char> gives to all life and breath and all things. <verse eid="ACT 17:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 17:26"/>And He made out of one <char style="add">man</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">17.26 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">out of one blood</char></note> every nation of men to dwell upon all the face of the earth, having determined the appointed times and the boundaries of their habitation, <verse eid="ACT 17:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 17:27"/>to seek God,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">17.27 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Lord</char></note> if perhaps indeed they might feel after Him and might find Him. And indeed, He is not far from each one of us. <verse eid="ACT 17:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 17:28"/>‘For in Him we live and move and are.’<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">17.28 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> This is probably a quote from the Cretan philosopher Epimenides of Knossos.</char></note> As also some of the poets among you⁺ have said, ‘For we are also <char style="add">His</char> offspring.’<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">17.28 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> This is probably a quote from the poem “Phainomena” by the Cilician philosopher Aratus.</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 17:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 17:29"/>Therefore, being offspring of God, we ought not to consider the Divine Being to be like gold or silver or stone, a graven thing of man’s craft and imagination. <verse eid="ACT 17:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 17:30"/>Indeed, therefore, God, having overlooked the times of ignorance, now commands all men everywhere to repent, <verse eid="ACT 17:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 17:31"/>because He set a day in which He is about to judge the world in righteousness by the Man whom He appointed, having provided a guarantee to all, having raised Him out from the dead.” <verse eid="ACT 17:31"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 17:32"/>Now having heard of a resurrection of the dead, some indeed began mocking, but some said, “We will hear you concerning this again also.” <verse eid="ACT 17:32"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 17:33"/>Thus Paul went out from their midst. <verse eid="ACT 17:33"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 17:34"/>But some men,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">17.34 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">some</char></note> having joined themselves to him, believed, among whom also <char style="add">were</char> Dionysius the Areopagite, and a woman named Damaris, and others with them. <verse eid="ACT 17:34"/></para>

<chapter eid="ACT 17"/>

<chapter number="18" style="c" sid="ACT 18"/>

<para style="s">Paul Ministers in Corinth</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 18:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">2 Corinthians 1:1–2</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">1 Corinthians 1:1–3</char></note>And after these things, having departed from Athens, he came to Corinth. <verse eid="ACT 18:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 18:2"/>And having found a certain Jew named Aquila, a native of Pontus, and Priscilla his wife, recently having come from Italy because of Claudius having commanded all the Jews to depart out of Rome, he came to them, <verse eid="ACT 18:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 18:3"/>and because of being of the same trade, he stayed with them and worked. For they were tentmakers by the trade. <verse eid="ACT 18:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 18:4"/>And he was reasoning in the synagogue on every Sabbath, persuading both Jews and Greeks. <verse eid="ACT 18:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 18:5"/>Now when both Silas and Timothy came down from Macedonia, Paul was occupied with the word, earnestly testifying to the Jews Jesus to be the Christ. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">18.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Paul was compelled by the Spirit</char></note><verse eid="ACT 18:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 18:6"/>But <char style="add">on</char> their opposing and reviling <char style="add">him</char>, having shaken out the garments, he said to them, “Your⁺ blood <char style="add">be</char> upon your⁺ head! I <char style="add">am</char> clean. From now on I will go to the Gentiles.” <verse eid="ACT 18:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 18:7"/>And having departed from there, he came to the house of a certain one named Titus Justus,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">18.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> ECM; NA, SBL, NE, and WH </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Titius Justus</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Justus</char></note> one worshiping God, whose house was adjoining the synagogue. <verse eid="ACT 18:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 18:8"/>And Crispus, the synagogue ruler, believed in the Lord with all his house, and many of the Corinthians hearing believed and were baptized. <verse eid="ACT 18:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 18:9"/>Now the Lord said to Paul through a vision in the night, <char style="wj">“Do not be afraid, but continue speaking, and do not be silent, </char><verse eid="ACT 18:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 18:10"/><char style="wj">because I am with you, and no one will lay a hand on you to harm you, because there are many people unto Me in this city.”</char> <verse eid="ACT 18:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 18:11"/>And he remained a year and six months, teaching the word of God among them. <verse eid="ACT 18:11"/></para>

<para style="s">Paul before Gallio</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 18:12"/>But Gallio being proconsul of Achaia, the Jews with one accord rose up against Paul and led him to the judgment seat, <verse eid="ACT 18:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 18:13"/>saying, “This <char style="add">man</char> persuades men to worship God contrary to the law.” <verse eid="ACT 18:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 18:14"/>And Paul being about to open the mouth, Gallio said to the Jews, “If indeed it was some unrighteousness or wicked crime, O Jews, according to reason I would have endured with you⁺. <verse eid="ACT 18:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 18:15"/>But if it is a question about a word and names and in reference to your⁺ law, you⁺ will see yourselves. I resolve<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">18.15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">For I resolve</char></note> not to be a judge of these things.” <verse eid="ACT 18:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 18:16"/>And he drove them from the judgment seat. <verse eid="ACT 18:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 18:17"/>Then they all,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">18.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">all the Greeks</char></note> having seized Sosthenes the synagogue ruler, were beating <char style="add">him</char> before the judgment seat. And it mattered nothing to Gallio about these things. <verse eid="ACT 18:17"/></para>

<para style="s">Paul Returns to Antioch</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 18:18"/>Now Paul, having remained many days more, having taken leave of the brothers, sailed away to Syria—and with him Priscilla and Aquila—having shaved the head in Cenchrea, for he had a vow. <verse eid="ACT 18:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 18:19"/>And they came<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">18.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">he came</char></note> to Ephesus and left them there. And he himself, having entered into the synagogue, reasoned with the Jews. <verse eid="ACT 18:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 18:20"/>And of them asking <char style="add">him</char> to remain<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">18.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">with them</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> for a longer time, he did not consent, <verse eid="ACT 18:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 18:21"/>but having taken leave and having said, “I will return<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">18.21 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">“It is necessary for me by all means to keep the coming feast in Jerusalem, but I will return</char></note> to you⁺ again, God willing,” he sailed from Ephesus, <verse eid="ACT 18:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 18:22"/>and having landed at Caesarea, having gone up and having greeted the church,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">18.22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the church at Jerusalem</char></note> he went down to Antioch. <verse eid="ACT 18:22"/></para>

<para style="s">Paul’s Third Missionary Journey BeginsActs 13:1–3</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 18:23"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Acts 15:36–41</char></note>And having stayed some time, he went out, passing successively through the Galatian region and Phrygia, strengthening all the disciples. <verse eid="ACT 18:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 18:24"/>Now a certain Jew named Apollos, a native of Alexandria, came to Ephesus, being an eloquent man, mighty in the Scriptures. <verse eid="ACT 18:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 18:25"/>He was instructed in the way of the Lord. And being fervent in spirit, he was speaking and was teaching earnestly the things concerning Jesus,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">18.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">concerning the Lord</char></note> knowing only the baptism of John, <verse eid="ACT 18:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 18:26"/>and he began to speak boldly in the synagogue. But Priscilla and Aquila,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">18.26 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Aquila and Priscilla</char></note> having heard him, took him to <char style="add">them</char> and expounded the way of God to him more accurately. <verse eid="ACT 18:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 18:27"/>And <char style="add">in</char> his resolving to pass through into Achaia, the brothers, having encouraged <char style="add">him</char>, wrote to the disciples to welcome him, who, having arrived, helped greatly those having believed through grace. <verse eid="ACT 18:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 18:28"/>For he was powerfully refuting the Jews publicly, showing by the Scriptures Jesus to be the Christ. <verse eid="ACT 18:28"/></para>

<chapter eid="ACT 18"/>

<chapter number="19" style="c" sid="ACT 19"/>

<para style="s">The Holy Spirit Received at Ephesus</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 19:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Acts 10:44–48</char></note>And it came to pass while Apollos was in Corinth <char style="add">that</char> Paul, having passed through the upper parts<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">19.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the highland</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the interior</char></note> to come to Ephesus and having found certain disciples, <verse eid="ACT 19:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 19:2"/>also said to them, “Did you⁺ receive the Holy Spirit, having believed?” </para>

<para style="p" vid="ACT 19:2">And <char style="add">they said</char> to him, “But we did not even hear that there is a Holy Spirit.” <verse eid="ACT 19:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 19:3"/>And he said, “Into what, then, were you⁺ baptized?” </para>

<para style="p" vid="ACT 19:3">And they said, “Into John's baptism.” <verse eid="ACT 19:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 19:4"/>And Paul said, “John<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">19.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">indeed</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> baptized a baptism of repentance, saying to the people that they should believe in the One coming after him, that is, in Jesus.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">19.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in Christ Jesus</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; GOC </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in Jesus Christ</char></note>” <verse eid="ACT 19:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 19:5"/>And having heard, they were baptized into the name of the Lord Jesus. <verse eid="ACT 19:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 19:6"/>And Paul having laid the hands on them, the Holy Spirit came upon them, and they were speaking in tongues and prophesying. <verse eid="ACT 19:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 19:7"/>And there were in all about twelve men. <verse eid="ACT 19:7"/></para>

<para style="s">Paul Ministers in EphesusEphesians 1:1–2</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 19:8"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Revelation 2:1–7</char></note>And having entered into the synagogue, he was speaking boldly for three months, reasoning and persuading concerning the kingdom of God. <verse eid="ACT 19:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 19:9"/>But when some were hardened and were disbelieving, speaking evil of the Way before the multitude, having departed from them, he separated the disciples, reasoning every day in the lecture hall of Tyrannus.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">19.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of a certain Tyrannus</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 19:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 19:10"/>And this continued for two years, so that all those inhabiting Asia<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">19.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the province of Asia</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; Asia was a Roman province in what is now western Turkey; similarly in verses 22, 26, 27, and 31.</char></note> heard the word of the Lord,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">19.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of the Lord Jesus</char></note> both Jews and Greeks. <verse eid="ACT 19:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 19:11"/>And God was doing miracles not being ordinary through the hands of Paul, <verse eid="ACT 19:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 19:12"/>so that even soudaria<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">19.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">handkerchiefs</char></note> or simikinthia<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">19.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">aprons worn by artisans</char></note> from his skin were brought to the ailing, and the diseases departed from them, and the evil spirits left. <verse eid="ACT 19:12"/></para>

<para style="s">Seven Sons of Sceva</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 19:13"/>And some of the itinerant Jews, exorcists, also attempted to invoke the name of the Lord Jesus over those having evil spirits, saying, “I adjure you⁺ <char style="add">by</char> Jesus, whom Paul proclaims.” <verse eid="ACT 19:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 19:14"/>Now seven sons of a certain Sceva, a Jewish high priest, were doing this. <verse eid="ACT 19:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 19:15"/>But the evil spirit, answering, said to them, “Jesus I know, and Paul I know about; but you⁺, who are you⁺?” <verse eid="ACT 19:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 19:16"/>And the man in whom was the evil spirit, having leapt on them, having overpowered them all,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">19.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">having overpowered them</char></note> prevailed against them so that they fled out of that house naked and wounded. <verse eid="ACT 19:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 19:17"/>Now this became known to all those inhabiting Ephesus, both Jews and Greeks. And fear fell upon them all, and the name of the Lord Jesus was being magnified. <verse eid="ACT 19:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 19:18"/>And many of those having believed were coming, confessing and declaring their deeds, <verse eid="ACT 19:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 19:19"/>and many of those having practiced works of magic, having brought the books, burned <char style="add">them</char> before all. And they counted up the prices of them and found <char style="add">it</char> five myriads of silver.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">19.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">fifty thousand drachmas.</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> A drachma was a silver coin worth about one day’s wages.</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 19:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 19:20"/>Thus the word of the Lord continued to increase and prevail with might. <verse eid="ACT 19:20"/></para>

<para style="s">The Riot in Ephesus</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 19:21"/>Now after these things were fulfilled, Paul purposed in the Spirit<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">19.21 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">purposed in his spirit</char></note> to go to Jerusalem, having passed through Macedonia and Achaia, having said, “After my having been there, it is necessary for me to see Rome also.” <verse eid="ACT 19:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 19:22"/>And having sent two of those ministering to him, Timothy and Erastus, into Macedonia, he remained for a time in Asia. <verse eid="ACT 19:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 19:23"/>And there arose at the same time no little disturbance<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">19.23 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">there arose a great disturbance</char></note> concerning the Way. <verse eid="ACT 19:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 19:24"/>For a certain silversmith named Demetrius, making silver shrines of Artemis, was bringing no little business<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">19.24 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">bringing much business</char></note> to the craftsmen. <verse eid="ACT 19:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 19:25"/>Having brought <char style="add">them</char> together along with the workmen in such things, he said, “Men, you⁺ know that out of this business is our wealth. <verse eid="ACT 19:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 19:26"/>And you⁺ see and hear that not only in Ephesus, but in almost all of Asia, this Paul, having persuaded <char style="add">them</char>, has turned away a great many people, saying that they are not gods being made by hands. <verse eid="ACT 19:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 19:27"/>Now not only is this business of ours endangered to come into disrepute, but also for the temple of the great goddess Artemis to be reckoned for nothing, and also her majesty to be deposed, whom all Asia and the world worship.” <verse eid="ACT 19:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 19:28"/>And having heard and having become full of rage, they were crying out, saying, “Great <char style="add">is</char> Artemis of the Ephesians!” <verse eid="ACT 19:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 19:29"/>And the city<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">19.29 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">all the city</char></note> was filled with confusion, and with one accord they rushed to the theatre, having dragged off Gaius and Aristarchus, Macedonians, fellow travelers of Paul. <verse eid="ACT 19:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 19:30"/>But on Paul intending to go in to the people, the disciples were not allowing him. <verse eid="ACT 19:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 19:31"/>And also some of the Asiarchs being friends to him,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">19.31 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">some of Paul's friends who were officials of the province of Asia</char></note> having sent to him, were urging him not to venture into the theatre. <verse eid="ACT 19:31"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 19:32"/>Some indeed therefore were crying out one thing, some <char style="add">another</char>. For the assembly was confused, and most did not know for what cause they were assembled. <verse eid="ACT 19:32"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 19:33"/>And out of the crowd they put forward Alexander, the Jews having thrust him forward. And Alexander, having motioned with the hand, was wanting to make a defense to the people. <verse eid="ACT 19:33"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 19:34"/>But having recognized that he is a Jew, there was one cry from all, ongoing about two hours, crying out, “Great <char style="add">is</char> Artemis of the Ephesians!” <verse eid="ACT 19:34"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 19:35"/>And having calmed the crowd, the town clerk says, “Men, Ephesians, what man is there indeed who does not know the city of the Ephesians as being temple-keeper of the great<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">19.35 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">goddess</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> Artemis and of that fallen from the sky? <verse eid="ACT 19:35"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 19:36"/>Therefore, these things being undeniable, it is necessary for you⁺ to be calm and to do nothing rash. <verse eid="ACT 19:36"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 19:37"/>For you⁺ brought these men, neither temple plunderers nor blaspheming our<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">19.37 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">your</char></note> goddess. <verse eid="ACT 19:37"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 19:38"/>Therefore if indeed Demetrius and the craftsmen with him have a matter against anyone, courts are conducted, and there are proconsuls; let them accuse one another. <verse eid="ACT 19:38"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="ACT 19:39"/>But if you⁺ inquire anything beyond this,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">19.39 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">anything concerning other matters</char></note> it will be solved in the lawful assembly. <verse eid="ACT 19:39"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="ACT 19:40"/>And indeed, we are in danger of being accused of insurrection concerning this day, there existing not one cause concerning which we will be able to give a reason concerning this commotion.” <verse eid="ACT 19:40"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="ACT 19:41"/>And having said these things, he dismissed the assembly. <verse eid="ACT 19:41"/></para>

<chapter eid="ACT 19"/>

<chapter number="20" style="c" sid="ACT 20"/>

<para style="s">Paul in Macedonia and Greece</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 20:1"/>Now after the uproar had ceased, Paul, having summoned the disciples and having encouraged <char style="add">them</char>,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR do not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">having encouraged them</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> having said farewell, went out to go to Macedonia. <verse eid="ACT 20:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 20:2"/>And having passed through those districts and having exhorted them with much talk, he came to Greece. <verse eid="ACT 20:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 20:3"/>And having continued three months, a plot having been made against him by the Jews, he being about to sail into Syria, a purpose arose to return through Macedonia. <verse eid="ACT 20:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 20:4"/>And he was accompanied<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">into Asia</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; Asia was a Roman province in what is now western Turkey; twice in this verse and also in verses 16 and 18.</char></note> by Sopater <char style="add">son</char> of Pyrrhus, a Berean,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Sopater of Berea</char></note> and Aristarchus, and Secundus of the Thessalonians, and Gaius of Derbe, and Timothy, and the Asians Tychicus and Trophimus. <verse eid="ACT 20:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 20:5"/>But these, having gone ahead, waited for us in Troas. <verse eid="ACT 20:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 20:6"/>And we sailed away from Philippi after the days of the Unleavened,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">after the Feast of Unleavened Bread</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; see Exodus 12:14–20.</char></note> and within five days we came to them at Troas, where we stayed seven days. <verse eid="ACT 20:6"/></para>

<para style="s">Eutychus Revived at Troas2 Kings 4:18–37</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 20:7"/>And on the first of the week, we having come together<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the disciples having come together</char></note> to break bread, Paul, about to depart on the next day, talked to them and continued the talk until midnight. <verse eid="ACT 20:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 20:8"/>Now there were many lamps in the upper room where we were<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">they were</char></note> assembled. <verse eid="ACT 20:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 20:9"/>And a certain young man named Eutychus was sitting by the window, overcome by deep sleep, Paul talking on longer. Having been overcome by sleep, he fell down from the third story and was picked up dead. <verse eid="ACT 20:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 20:10"/>But Paul, having descended, fell upon him, and having embraced <char style="add">him</char>, he said, “Do not be alarmed, for his life is in him!” <verse eid="ACT 20:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 20:11"/>And having gone up, and having broken the bread, and having eaten, and having talked for a considerable <char style="add">time</char> until daybreak, so he went out. <verse eid="ACT 20:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 20:12"/>Then they brought the boy alive and were not just a little comforted. <verse eid="ACT 20:12"/></para>

<para style="s">From Troas to Miletus</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 20:13"/>But we, having gone ahead to<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ </char><char style="fq" closed="false">having gone to</char></note> the ship, sailed to Assos, being about to take in Paul there. For having arranged thus, he was readying himself to go on foot. <verse eid="ACT 20:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 20:14"/>And when he met with us at Assos, having taken him in, we came to Mitylene. <verse eid="ACT 20:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 20:15"/>And having sailed away from there, the next day we arrived opposite Chios, and the second <char style="add">day</char> we arrived at Samos, and<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20.15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and, having remained at Trogyllium,</char></note> the following <char style="add">day</char> we came to Miletus. <verse eid="ACT 20:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 20:16"/>For Paul had decided to sail by Ephesus, so that it might not come upon him to spend time in Asia; for he was hastening, if it was possible for him, to be in Jerusalem on the day of Pentecost.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, Shavuot, the late spring feast of pilgrimage to Jerusalem; it is also known as </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Feast of Harvest</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> (see Exodus 23:16) or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Feast of Weeks</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> (see Exodus 34:22).</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 20:16"/></para>

<para style="s">Paul’s Farewell to the Ephesians</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 20:17"/>And from Miletus, having sent to Ephesus, he called for the elders of the church. <verse eid="ACT 20:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 20:18"/>And when they had come to him, he said to them, “You⁺ know from the first day on which I arrived in Asia, how I was with you⁺ the whole time, <verse eid="ACT 20:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 20:19"/>serving the Lord with all humility and tears,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and many tears</char></note> and in trials having befallen me in the plots of the Jews; <verse eid="ACT 20:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 20:20"/>how I kept back nothing of that being profitable, to declare <char style="add">it</char> to you⁺ and to teach you⁺ publicly and from house to house, <verse eid="ACT 20:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 20:21"/>earnestly testifying both to the Jews and to the Greeks repentance to God and faith in our Lord Jesus Christ.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20.21 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> ECM, TR, GOC, and Tischendorf; NA, SBL, NE, BYZ, and WH </char><char style="fq" closed="false">our Lord Jesus</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 20:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 20:22"/>And now behold, bound in the Spirit I go to Jerusalem, not knowing what will happen to me in it, <verse eid="ACT 20:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 20:23"/>except that the Holy Spirit fully testifies to me<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20.23 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR do not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to me</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> in every city, saying that chains and tribulations await me. <verse eid="ACT 20:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 20:24"/>But on no account do I make my life dear to myself, so as to finish my course<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20.24 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">with joy</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> and the ministry that I received from the Lord Jesus: to testify fully to the gospel of the grace of God. <verse eid="ACT 20:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 20:25"/>And now, behold, I know that all of you⁺ among whom I went about proclaiming the kingdom will see my face no more. <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of God</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note><verse eid="ACT 20:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 20:26"/>Therefore I testify to you⁺ in this day that I <char style="add">am</char> innocent of the blood of all.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20.26 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> See Ezekiel 33:8–9.</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 20:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 20:27"/>For I did not shrink back from proclaiming to you⁺ the whole counsel of God. <verse eid="ACT 20:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 20:28"/>Take heed<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20.28 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">therefore</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> to yourselves and to all the flock among whom the Holy Spirit has set you⁺ as overseers, to shepherd the church of God,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20.28 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Tischendorf </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of the Lord</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; BYZ and GOC </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of the Lord and God</char></note> which He purchased with <char style="add">His</char> own blood. <verse eid="ACT 20:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 20:29"/>I have known that<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20.29 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">For I have known this, that</char></note> after my departure, grievous wolves will come in among you⁺, not sparing the flock, <verse eid="ACT 20:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 20:30"/>and out from your⁺ own selves men will rise up, speaking perverse things to draw away disciples after them. <verse eid="ACT 20:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 20:31"/>Therefore stay awake, remembering that three years, night and day, I did not cease admonishing each one with tears. <verse eid="ACT 20:31"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 20:32"/>And now I commit you⁺<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">20.32 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">brothers</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> to God and to the word of His grace, being able to build <char style="add">you</char> up and to give you an inheritance among all those having been sanctified. <verse eid="ACT 20:32"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 20:33"/>I coveted no one’s silver or gold or clothing. <verse eid="ACT 20:33"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 20:34"/>You yourselves know that these hands ministered to my needs and to those being with me. <verse eid="ACT 20:34"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 20:35"/>In everything I showed you⁺ that by thus laboring, it is necessary to aid those being weak, and also to remember the words of the Lord Jesus, how He Himself said, <char style="wj">‘It is more blessed to give than to receive.’</char>” <verse eid="ACT 20:35"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 20:36"/>And having said these things, having bowed his knee, he prayed with them all. <verse eid="ACT 20:36"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 20:37"/>Then there was much weeping among all, and having fallen upon the neck of Paul, they were kissing him, <verse eid="ACT 20:37"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 20:38"/>sorrowing especially over the word that he had spoken, that they are about to see his face no more. And they accompanied him to the ship. <verse eid="ACT 20:38"/></para>

<chapter eid="ACT 20"/>

<chapter number="21" style="c" sid="ACT 21"/>

<para style="s">Paul’s Journey to Jerusalem</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 21:1"/>And it happened that after having drawn away from them, having run directly in our sailing, we came to Cos, and the next day to Rhodes, and from there to Patara. <verse eid="ACT 21:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 21:2"/>And having found a boat passing over into Phoenicia, having gone aboard, we set sail. <verse eid="ACT 21:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 21:3"/>And having sighted Cyprus and having left it on the left, we kept sailing to Syria and landed at Tyre, for the ship was unloading the cargo there. <verse eid="ACT 21:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 21:4"/>And we remained there seven days, having sought out the disciples,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">21.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">having sought out disciples</char></note> who kept saying to Paul through the Spirit not to go up to Jerusalem. <verse eid="ACT 21:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 21:5"/>And it happened that when we had completed the days, having gone out, we journeyed, all accompanying us, with wives and children, as far as outside the city. And having bowed the knees on the shore, having prayed, <verse eid="ACT 21:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 21:6"/>having said farewell to one another, we then went up into the boat, and they returned to their own. <verse eid="ACT 21:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 21:7"/>And having completed the voyage from Tyre, we came down to Ptolemais; and having greeted the brothers, we stayed one day with them. <verse eid="ACT 21:7"/></para>

<para style="s">Paul Visits Philip the Evangelist</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 21:8"/>And having gone out on the next day, we came to<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">21.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Paul and his companions came to</char></note> Caesarea; and having entered into the house of Philip the evangelist, being of the Seven,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">21.8 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> See Acts 6:5.</char></note> we stayed with him. <verse eid="ACT 21:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 21:9"/>And with this <char style="add">man</char> there were four daughters, virgins, prophesying. <verse eid="ACT 21:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 21:10"/>And <char style="add">in our</char> remaining many days, a certain prophet named Agabus came down from Judea. <verse eid="ACT 21:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 21:11"/>And having come to us and having taken Paul’s belt, having bound his feet and hands,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">21.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">hands and feet</char></note> he said, “Thus the Holy Spirit says, ‘In this way the Jews in Jerusalem will bind the man whose belt this is, and they will deliver <char style="add">him</char> into the hands of the Gentiles.’” <verse eid="ACT 21:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 21:12"/>And when we had heard these things, both we and those of that place were begging him not to go up to Jerusalem. <verse eid="ACT 21:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 21:13"/>Then Paul answered, “What are you⁺ doing, weeping and breaking my heart? For I have readiness not only to be bound, but also to die at Jerusalem for the name of the Lord Jesus.” <verse eid="ACT 21:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 21:14"/>And he not being persuaded, we were silent, having said, “The will of the Lord be done.” <verse eid="ACT 21:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 21:15"/>And after these days, having packed the baggage, we were going up to Jerusalem. <verse eid="ACT 21:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 21:16"/>And some of the disciples from Caesarea also went with us, bringing a certain Mnason, a Cypriot, an early disciple with whom we would lodge. <verse eid="ACT 21:16"/></para>

<para style="s">Paul’s Arrival at Jerusalem</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 21:17"/>Now of us having arrived at Jerusalem, the brothers received us gladly. <verse eid="ACT 21:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 21:18"/>And on the following <char style="add">day</char>, Paul went in with us to James, and all the elders arrived. <verse eid="ACT 21:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 21:19"/>And having greeted them, he began to relate, one by one, each of the things God had done among the Gentiles through his ministry. <verse eid="ACT 21:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 21:20"/>And those having heard were glorifying God,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">21.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">glorifying the Lord</char></note> and they said to him, “You see, brother, how many myriads there are among the Jews having believed, and they are all zealous ones of the law. <verse eid="ACT 21:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 21:21"/>Now they have been informed about you that you teach all Jews among the Gentiles apostasy from Moses, telling them not to circumcise the children nor to walk in the customs. <verse eid="ACT 21:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 21:22"/>What then is it? Certainly<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">21.22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">a multitude will gather, for</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> they will hear that you have come. <verse eid="ACT 21:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 21:23"/>Therefore do this that we say to you. With us there are four men having a vow on themselves. <verse eid="ACT 21:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 21:24"/>Having taken these, be purified with them and bear expense for them, so that they will shave the head. And all will know that what they have been informed about you is nothing, but <char style="add">that</char> you yourself also walk orderly, keeping the law. <verse eid="ACT 21:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 21:25"/>Now concerning those of the Gentiles having believed, we wrote, having adjudged,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">21.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">that they should observe no such thing, except</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> to keep themselves from both the things sacrificed to idols and blood, and <char style="add">from</char> what is strangled and sexual immorality.” <verse eid="ACT 21:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 21:26"/>Then Paul, having taken the men on the following day, having been purified with them, entered into the temple, declaring the fulfillment of the days of the purification until the offering was offered for each one of them. <verse eid="ACT 21:26"/></para>

<para style="s">Paul Seized at the Temple</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 21:27"/>Now when the seven days were about to be completed, the Jews from Asia,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">21.27 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">from the province of Asia</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; Asia was a Roman province in what is now western Turkey. </char></note> having seen him in the temple, began stirring up all the crowd, and they laid the hands upon him, <verse eid="ACT 21:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 21:28"/>crying out, “Men, Israelites, help! This is the man who <char style="add">is</char> teaching all those everywhere against the people and the law and this place. And besides, he has also brought Greeks into the temple and defiled this holy place.” <verse eid="ACT 21:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 21:29"/>For it was they having previously seen<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">21.29 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ </char><char style="fq" closed="false">having seen</char></note> Trophimus the Ephesian in the city with him, whom they were supposing that Paul had brought into the temple. <verse eid="ACT 21:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 21:30"/>And the whole city was provoked, and there was a rushing together of the people. And having laid hold of Paul, they dragged him outside the temple, and immediately the doors were shut. <verse eid="ACT 21:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 21:31"/>And <char style="add">in</char> their seeking to kill him, a report came to the commander of the cohort<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">21.31 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the commander of the Roman regiment</char></note> that all Jerusalem was in an uproar, <verse eid="ACT 21:31"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 21:32"/>who at once, having taken with <char style="add">him</char> soldiers and centurions, ran down upon them. And having seen the commander and the soldiers, they stopped beating Paul. <verse eid="ACT 21:32"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 21:33"/>Then having drawn near, the commander laid hold of him and commanded <char style="add">him</char> to be bound with two chains, and he began inquiring who he might be and what it is he has been doing. <verse eid="ACT 21:33"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 21:34"/>They were crying out in the crowd one thing, but others another. And he, not being able to know the facts on account of the uproar, ordered him to be brought into the barracks. <verse eid="ACT 21:34"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 21:35"/>And when he came to the stairs, it happened that he was carried by the soldiers because of the violence of the crowd. <verse eid="ACT 21:35"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 21:36"/>For the multitude of the people were following, crying out, “Away with him!” <verse eid="ACT 21:36"/></para>

<para style="s">Paul Addresses the Crowd</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 21:37"/>And being about to be brought into the barracks, Paul says to the commander, “Is it permitted to me to say something to you?<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">21.37 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to speak to you</char></note>” And he was saying, “Do you know Greek? <verse eid="ACT 21:37"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 21:38"/>Are you not, then, the Egyptian, the one before these days having led a revolt and having led out into the wilderness<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">21.38 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">desert</char></note> the four thousand men of the Assassins?” <verse eid="ACT 21:38"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="ACT 21:39"/>But Paul said, “I am indeed a Jew, a man of Tarsus of Cilicia, a citizen <char style="add">of</char> no insignificant city. Now I implore you, allow me to speak to the people.” <verse eid="ACT 21:39"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="ACT 21:40"/>And he having allowed <char style="add">him</char>, Paul, having stood on the stairs, made a sign with the hand to the people. And a great silence having taken place, he spoke to <char style="add">them</char> in the Hebrew language,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">21.40 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in the Aramaic language</char></note> saying: <verse eid="ACT 21:40"/></para>

<chapter eid="ACT 21"/>

<chapter number="22" style="c" sid="ACT 22"/>

<para style="s">Paul’s Defense to the Crowd</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 22:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Acts 26:1–23</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Acts 9:1–19</char></note>“Men, brothers and fathers, hear now my defense to you⁺.” <verse eid="ACT 22:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 22:2"/>And having heard that he was addressing them in the Hebrew language,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">22.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in the Aramaic language</char></note> they became even more quiet. And he says, <verse eid="ACT 22:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 22:3"/>“I am<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">22.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">indeed</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> a man, a Jew, born in Tarsus of Cilicia and brought up in this city at the feet of Gamaliel, having been educated according to the exactness of the law of our fathers, being a zealous one of God, even as all of you⁺ are this day, <verse eid="ACT 22:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 22:4"/>who persecuted this Way as far as death, binding and delivering to prisons both men and women, <verse eid="ACT 22:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 22:5"/>as also the high priest—and all the elderhood—testifies to me, from whom also having received letters to the brothers, I was going to Damascus to bring also those being there bound to Jerusalem so that they might be punished. <verse eid="ACT 22:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 22:6"/>But it happened to me, journeying and drawing near to Damascus about noon, <char style="add">that</char> suddenly a great light out of heaven shone around me, <verse eid="ACT 22:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 22:7"/>and I fell to the ground and heard a voice saying to me, <char style="wj">‘Saul, Saul, why do you persecute Me?’</char> <verse eid="ACT 22:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 22:8"/>And I answered, ‘Who are You, Lord?’ And He said to me, <char style="wj">‘I am Jesus of Nazareth, whom you are persecuting.’</char> <verse eid="ACT 22:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 22:9"/>And those being with me indeed saw the light,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">22.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and were terrified</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> but they did not hear the voice of the One speaking to me. <verse eid="ACT 22:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 22:10"/>And I said, ‘What shall I do, Lord?’ </para>

<para style="p" vid="ACT 22:10">And the Lord said to me, <char style="wj">‘Having risen up, go to Damascus, and there it will be told to you concerning all things that it has been appointed to you to do.’</char> <verse eid="ACT 22:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 22:11"/>And while I could not see from the brightness of that light, I came to Damascus, being led by the hand by those being with me. <verse eid="ACT 22:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 22:12"/>And a certain Ananias, a devout man according to the law, being testified to by all the Jews dwelling <char style="add">there</char>,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">22.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> GOC, HF, and F35 </char><char style="fq" closed="false">dwelling in Damascus</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 22:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 22:13"/>having come to me and having stood near, said to me, ‘Brother Saul, look up.’ And the same hour I looked up at him. <verse eid="ACT 22:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 22:14"/>And he said, ‘The God of our fathers has appointed you to know His will, and to see the Righteous One, and to hear a voice out of His mouth. <verse eid="ACT 22:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 22:15"/>For you will be a witness for Him to all men of what you have seen and heard. <verse eid="ACT 22:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 22:16"/>And now, why do you delay? Having arisen, be baptized and wash away your sins, having called on His name.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">22.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">on the name of the Lord</char></note>’ <verse eid="ACT 22:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 22:17"/>And it happened to me, having returned to Jerusalem and <char style="add">in</char> my praying in the temple, <char style="add">that</char> I fell into a trance <verse eid="ACT 22:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 22:18"/>and saw Him<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">22.18 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">saw the Lord</char></note> saying to me, <char style="wj">‘Make haste and go forth with speed out of Jerusalem, because they will not accept your testimony about Me.’</char> <verse eid="ACT 22:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 22:19"/>And I said, ‘Lord, they themselves know that in each of those synagogues I was imprisoning and beating those believing on You. <verse eid="ACT 22:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 22:20"/>And when the blood of Your witness<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">22.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">martyr</char></note> Stephen was poured out, I myself was also standing by and consenting<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">22.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to his death</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> and watching over the garments of those killing him.’ <verse eid="ACT 22:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 22:21"/>And He said to me, <char style="wj">‘Go, because I will send you far away to the Gentiles.’</char>” <verse eid="ACT 22:21"/></para>

<para style="s">Paul the Roman Citizen</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 22:22"/>Now they were listening to him until this word. And they lifted up their voice, saying, “Away with such from the earth! For it is not fitting <char style="add">for</char> him to live!” <verse eid="ACT 22:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 22:23"/>And <char style="add">in</char> their crying out and casting off the garments and throwing dust into the air, <verse eid="ACT 22:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 22:24"/>the commander ordered him to be brought into the barracks, having directed him to be examined by flogging, so that he might know for what cause they were crying out against him like this. <verse eid="ACT 22:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 22:25"/>But as they stretched him forward<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">22.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> RP and Stephanus TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">as he stretched him forward</char></note> with the straps, Paul said to the centurion standing by, “Is it lawful to you⁺ to flog a man <char style="add">who is</char> a Roman and uncondemned?” <verse eid="ACT 22:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 22:26"/>And the centurion, having heard, having gone to the commander, reported <char style="add">it</char>, saying, “What are you about to do?<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">22.26 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">“Consider what you are about to do.”</char></note> For this man is a Roman.” <verse eid="ACT 22:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 22:27"/>And having come near, the commander said to him, “Tell me, are you a Roman?” </para>

<para style="p" vid="ACT 22:27">And he was saying, “Yes.” <verse eid="ACT 22:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 22:28"/>And the commander answered, “I bought this citizenship with a great sum.” </para>

<para style="p" vid="ACT 22:28">But Paul was saying, “But I have even been born <char style="add">so</char>.” <verse eid="ACT 22:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 22:29"/>So immediately those being about to examine him departed from him, and the commander also was afraid, having ascertained that he is a Roman, and because he had bound him. <verse eid="ACT 22:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 22:30"/>And on the next day, desiring to know for certain why he is accused by the Jews, he unbound him<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">22.30 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">from the bonds</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> and he commanded the chief priests and all the Council<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">22.30 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the whole Sanhedrin</char></note> to assemble. And having brought down Paul, he set <char style="add">him</char> among them. <verse eid="ACT 22:30"/></para>

<chapter eid="ACT 22"/>

<chapter number="23" style="c" sid="ACT 23"/>

<para style="s">Paul before the Sanhedrin</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 23:1"/>And having looked intently at the Council,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">23.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Sanhedrin</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; also in verses 6, 15, 20, and 28</char></note> Paul said, “Men, brothers, I have conducted myself in all good conscience to God up to this day.” <verse eid="ACT 23:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 23:2"/>And the high priest Ananias commanded those standing by him to strike him on the mouth. <verse eid="ACT 23:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 23:3"/>Then Paul said to him, “God is about to strike you, whitewashed wall! And you, do you sit judging me according to the law, and violating the law, command me to be struck?” <verse eid="ACT 23:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 23:4"/>But those who stood by said, “Do you insult the high priest of God?” <verse eid="ACT 23:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 23:5"/>And Paul was saying, “I was not aware, brothers, that he is high priest; for it has been written: ‘You shall not speak evil <char style="add">of</char> the ruler of your people.’” <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">23.5 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Exodus 22:28 (see also LXX)</char></note><verse eid="ACT 23:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 23:6"/>And Paul, having known that the one part consists of Sadducees, but the other of Pharisees,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">23.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> F35 </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Pharisees, but the other of Sadducees</char></note> was crying out in the Council, “Men, brothers, I am a Pharisee, the son of a Pharisee; concerning hope and resurrection of the dead I am judged.” <verse eid="ACT 23:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 23:7"/>And <char style="add">on</char> his saying this, a dissension arose between the Pharisees and Sadducees,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">23.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> RP does not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and Sadducees</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> and the multitude was divided. <verse eid="ACT 23:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 23:8"/>For indeed Sadducees say there is no resurrection nor angel nor spirit, but Pharisees confess both. <verse eid="ACT 23:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 23:9"/>Then a great clamor arose, and some of the scribes of the party of the Pharisees, having risen up, were contending, saying, “We find nothing evil in this man. And <char style="add">what</char> if a spirit or an angel has spoken to him?<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">23.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">And if a spirit or an angel has spoken to him, let us not fight against God</char></note>” <verse eid="ACT 23:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 23:10"/>And a great dissension arising, the commander, having feared, lest Paul should be torn to pieces by them, commanded the troop, having gone down, to take him by force from their midst and to bring <char style="add">him</char> into the barracks. <verse eid="ACT 23:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 23:11"/>But the following night the Lord, having stood by him, said, <char style="wj">“Take courage,</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">23.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Paul</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note><char style="wj"> for as you have fully testified about Me at Jerusalem, so also it is necessary for you to testify at Rome.”</char> <verse eid="ACT 23:11"/></para>

<para style="s">The Plot to Kill PaulJohn 16:1–4</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 23:12"/>And day having come, the Jews,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">23.12 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">some of the Jews</char></note> having made a conspiracy, put themselves under an oath, declaring neither to eat nor to drink until they should kill Paul. <verse eid="ACT 23:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 23:13"/>Now there were more than forty having made this sworn conspiracy, <verse eid="ACT 23:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 23:14"/>who, having come to the chief priests and the elders, said, “We have bound ourselves with an oath to eat nothing until we should kill Paul. <verse eid="ACT 23:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 23:15"/>Now therefore, you⁺, with the Council, make a report to the commander, so that<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">23.15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">tomorrow</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> he might bring him down to you⁺ as being about to examine more accurately the things about him. And we are ready to kill him before his drawing near.” <verse eid="ACT 23:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 23:16"/>But the son of Paul’s sister, having heard of the ambush,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">23.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the plot</char></note> having come near and having entered into the barracks, reported <char style="add">it</char> to Paul. <verse eid="ACT 23:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 23:17"/>And Paul, having summoned one of the centurions, was saying, “Take this young man to the commander, for he has something to report to him.” <verse eid="ACT 23:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 23:18"/>Therefore indeed the one having taken him brought <char style="add">him</char> to the commander, and he says, “Paul the prisoner, having summoned me, asked <char style="add">me</char> to lead this young man to you, having something to say to you.” <verse eid="ACT 23:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 23:19"/>Then the commander, having taken hold of his hand and having withdrawn in private, began to inquire, “What is it that you have to report to me?” <verse eid="ACT 23:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 23:20"/>And he said, “The Jews have agreed to ask you that you might bring down Paul into the Council tomorrow as being about to inquire something more accurately about him. <verse eid="ACT 23:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 23:21"/>You, therefore, should not be persuaded by them. For more than forty of their men lie in wait for him, who have put themselves under an oath neither to eat nor to drink until they should kill him; and now they are ready, awaiting the promise from you.” <verse eid="ACT 23:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 23:22"/>Therefore indeed the commander dismissed the young man, having instructed <char style="add">him</char>, “Tell no one that you have reported these things to me.” <verse eid="ACT 23:22"/></para>

<para style="s">Paul Sent to Felix</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 23:23"/>And having summoned a certain two of the centurions, he said, “Prepare for the third hour of the night<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">23.23 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, at nine tonight</char></note> two hundred soldiers and seventy horsemen and two hundred spearmen, so that they might go as far as Caesarea, <verse eid="ACT 23:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 23:24"/>and provide mounts so that, having set Paul upon <char style="add">them</char>, they might bring <char style="add">him</char> safely to Felix the governor,” <verse eid="ACT 23:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 23:25"/>having written a letter having this form: <verse eid="ACT 23:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 23:26"/>Claudius Lysias, </para>

<para style="p" vid="ACT 23:26">To the most excellent Governor Felix: </para>

<para style="p" vid="ACT 23:26">Greetings. <verse eid="ACT 23:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 23:27"/>This man having been seized by the Jews and being about to be killed by them—having come up with the troop, I rescued <char style="add">him</char>, having learned that he is a Roman. <verse eid="ACT 23:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 23:28"/>And resolving to know the charge on account of which they were accusing him, I brought <char style="add">him</char> down to their Council, <verse eid="ACT 23:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 23:29"/>whom I found being accused concerning questions of their law, but having no accusation worthy of death or of chains. <verse eid="ACT 23:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 23:30"/>And a plot<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">23.30 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">by the Jews</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> having been disclosed to me to be against the man, I sent <char style="add">him</char> to you at once, also having instructed the accusers to speak these things against him before you.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">23.30 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Farewell</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 23:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 23:31"/>Therefore indeed the soldiers, according to that having been ordered them, having taken Paul, brought <char style="add">him</char> to Antipatris by night. <verse eid="ACT 23:31"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 23:32"/>And on the next day, having allowed the horsemen to go with him, they returned to the barracks; <verse eid="ACT 23:32"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 23:33"/>those having entered into Caesarea and having delivered the letter to the governor, also presented Paul to him. <verse eid="ACT 23:33"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 23:34"/>And having read <char style="add">it</char> and having asked what province he is from, and having learned that <char style="add">he is</char> from Cilicia, <verse eid="ACT 23:34"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 23:35"/>he was saying, “I will hear you fully when your accusers may have arrived also,” having commanded him to be guarded in the Praetorium of Herod. <verse eid="ACT 23:35"/></para>

<chapter eid="ACT 23"/>

<chapter number="24" style="c" sid="ACT 24"/>

<para style="s">Tertullus Prosecutes Paul</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 24:1"/>And after five days the high priest Ananias came down with some elders<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">24.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">with the elders</char></note> and a certain orator,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">24.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">lawyer</char></note> Tertullus, who made a presentation against Paul to the governor. <verse eid="ACT 24:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 24:2"/>And he having been called, Tertullus began to accuse <char style="add">him</char>, saying, “Attaining great peace through you, and excellent measures<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">24.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">worthy deeds</char></note> being done to this nation through your foresight, <verse eid="ACT 24:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 24:3"/>in every way and also everywhere, we gladly accept <char style="add">it</char>, most excellent Felix, with all thankfulness. <verse eid="ACT 24:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 24:4"/>But so that I should not be a hindrance to you any longer, I implore you to hear us briefly <char style="add">in</char> your kindness. <verse eid="ACT 24:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 24:5"/>For having found this man a pestilence and stirring dissension among all the Jews in the world—also a leader of the sect of the Nazarenes— <verse eid="ACT 24:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 24:6"/>who even attempted to profane the temple, whom we also seized.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">24.6 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> TR includes </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and we wanted to judge him according to our law. </char><char style="fq" closed="false">7</char><char style="fq" closed="false">But Lysias the commander, having come up with much force, took him away out of our hands, </char><char style="fq" closed="false">8</char><char style="fq" closed="false">having commanded his accusers to come to you.</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 24:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 24:8"/>Having examined <char style="add">him</char> yourself, you will be able to know from him concerning all these things of which we accuse him.” <verse eid="ACT 24:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 24:9"/>And the Jews also agreed, declaring these things to be so. <verse eid="ACT 24:9"/></para>

<para style="s">Paul’s Defense to Felix</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 24:10"/>And the governor having motioned to him to speak, Paul answered: “Knowing you as being a judge<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">24.10 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> F35 </char><char style="fq" closed="false">a righteous judge</char></note> to this nation for many years, I make a defense cheerfully to the things concerning myself, <verse eid="ACT 24:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 24:11"/>you being able to know that there are to me no more than twelve days since I went up to worship in Jerusalem. <verse eid="ACT 24:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 24:12"/>And neither did they find me reasoning with anyone or making a tumultuous gathering of a crowd in the temple, nor in the synagogues, nor in the city. <verse eid="ACT 24:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 24:13"/>Nor are they able to prove to you<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">24.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR do not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to you</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> <char style="add">the things</char> concerning which now they accuse me. <verse eid="ACT 24:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 24:14"/>But I confess this to you, that according to the Way, which they call a sect, so I serve the God of our fathers, believing all things throughout the Law and that have been written in the Prophets, <verse eid="ACT 24:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 24:15"/>having a hope in God, which they themselves also await, <char style="add">that</char> there is about to be a resurrection<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">24.15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of the dead</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> both of righteous and of unrighteous. <verse eid="ACT 24:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 24:16"/>In this I myself also strive to have a conscience without offense toward God and men through everything. <verse eid="ACT 24:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 24:17"/>Now after many years, I arrived to bring alms to my nation, and offerings, <verse eid="ACT 24:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 24:18"/>during which they found me purified in the temple, not with a crowd nor with an uproar. But <char style="add">there are</char> some Jews from Asia<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">24.18 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">from the province of Asia</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; Asia was a Roman province in what is now western Turkey. </char></note> <verse eid="ACT 24:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 24:19"/>who ought to appear before you and to make accusation if they may have anything against me. <verse eid="ACT 24:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 24:20"/>Or let these say themselves any unrighteousness they found<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">24.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in me</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> in my having stood before the Council,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">24.20 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Sanhedrin</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 24:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 24:21"/>other than concerning this one voice in which I cried out standing among them: ‘I am judged by you⁺ this day concerning the resurrection of the dead.’” <verse eid="ACT 24:21"/></para>

<para style="s">The Verdict Postponed</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 24:22"/>But<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">24.22 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">on hearing these things</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> Felix, having known more precisely the things concerning the Way, put them off, having said, “When Lysias the commander shall have come down, I will examine the things as to you⁺,” <verse eid="ACT 24:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 24:23"/>having commanded the centurion to keep him and to <char style="add">let him</char> have ease and not to forbid his own to minister<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">24.23 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to come and minister</char></note> to him. <verse eid="ACT 24:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 24:24"/>Then after some days Felix, having arrived with <char style="add">his</char> own wife Drusilla, being a Jewess, sent for Paul and heard him concerning the faith in Christ Jesus.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">24.24 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in Christ</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 24:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 24:25"/>And <char style="add">in</char> his reasoning concerning righteousness and self-control and the coming judgment, Felix, having become frightened, answered, “Be going for the present, and having found opportunity, I will call for you,” <verse eid="ACT 24:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 24:26"/>at the same time also hoping that riches will be given to him by Paul.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">24.26 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">to release him</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> Therefore also, sending for him often, he was talking with him. <verse eid="ACT 24:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 24:27"/>But two years having been completed, Felix received Porcius Festus <char style="add">as</char> successor, and wishing to acquire for himself favor with the Jews, Felix left Paul bound. <verse eid="ACT 24:27"/></para>

<chapter eid="ACT 24"/>

<chapter number="25" style="c" sid="ACT 25"/>

<para style="s">Paul’s Trial before Festus</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 25:1"/>Therefore Festus, having arrived in the province, after three days went up to Jerusalem from Caesarea. <verse eid="ACT 25:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 25:2"/>And the chief priests and the chiefs of the Jews presented to him against Paul, and they were imploring him, <verse eid="ACT 25:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 25:3"/>requesting a favor against him that he would summon him to Jerusalem, forming an ambush to kill him on the way. <verse eid="ACT 25:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 25:4"/>Then, indeed, Festus answered that Paul is to be kept in Caesarea, and <char style="add">that</char> he himself is about to go out in haste. <verse eid="ACT 25:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 25:5"/>“Therefore those powerful among you⁺,” he says, “having gone down together, if there is anything wrong in the man, let them accuse him.” <verse eid="ACT 25:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 25:6"/>And having spent with them no more than eight or ten days, having gone down to Caesarea, on the next day having sat on the judgment seat, he commanded Paul to be brought. <verse eid="ACT 25:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 25:7"/>And he having arrived, the Jews having come down from Jerusalem stood around him, bringing many and weighty charges, which they were not able to prove. <verse eid="ACT 25:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 25:8"/>Paul made his defense: “Neither against the law of the Jews, nor against the temple, nor against Caesar, have I sinned <char style="add">in</char> anything.” <verse eid="ACT 25:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 25:9"/>But Festus, wishing to lay a favor on the Jews, answering, said to Paul, “Are you willing, having gone up to Jerusalem, to be judged before me there concerning these things?” <verse eid="ACT 25:9"/></para>

<para style="s">Paul Appeals to Caesar</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 25:10"/>And Paul said, “I am standing before the judgment seat of Caesar, where it is necessary for me to be judged. I did nothing wrong to the Jews, as you also know very well. <verse eid="ACT 25:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 25:11"/>Therefore if indeed I am unrighteous and have done anything worthy of death, I do not refuse to die. But if there is nothing of which they can accuse me, no one can give me up to them. I appeal to Caesar!” <verse eid="ACT 25:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 25:12"/>Then Festus, having conferred with the council, answered, “You have appealed to Caesar; to Caesar you will go!” <verse eid="ACT 25:12"/></para>

<para style="s">Festus Consults Agrippa</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 25:13"/>Now some days having passed, Agrippa the king and Bernice came down to Caesarea, greeting Festus. <verse eid="ACT 25:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 25:14"/>And as they were staying there many days, Festus laid before the king the things relating to Paul, saying, “There is a certain man left by Felix, a prisoner, <verse eid="ACT 25:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 25:15"/>concerning whom, <char style="add">in</char> my having been in Jerusalem, the chief priests and the elders of the Jews made a presentation, requesting a judgment against him, <verse eid="ACT 25:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 25:16"/>to whom I answered that it is not a custom with Romans to give up any man before the one being accused may have <char style="add">it</char> to face the accusers and may have a place of defense concerning the accusation. <verse eid="ACT 25:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 25:17"/>Therefore <char style="add">on</char> their having come together here, having made no delay, the next day having sat on the judgment seat, I commanded the man to be brought, <verse eid="ACT 25:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 25:18"/>concerning whom the accusers, having stood up, were bringing no charge of the evils that I was expecting. <verse eid="ACT 25:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 25:19"/>But they had certain questions against him concerning <char style="add">their</char> own religion and concerning a certain Jesus having been dead, whom Paul was affirming to be alive. <verse eid="ACT 25:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 25:20"/>Now I, being perplexed concerning this inquiry, was asking if he was willing to go to Jerusalem and there to be judged concerning these things. <verse eid="ACT 25:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 25:21"/>But Paul having appealed for himself to be kept for the decision of the Emperor, I commanded him to be kept until I might send him to Caesar.” <verse eid="ACT 25:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 25:22"/>And Agrippa <char style="add">said</char> to Festus, “I have also been wanting to hear the man myself.” </para>

<para style="p" vid="ACT 25:22">He says, “Tomorrow you will hear him.” <verse eid="ACT 25:22"/></para>

<para style="s">Paul before Agrippa and Bernice</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 25:23"/>Therefore on the next day, Agrippa and Bernice having come with great pomp and having entered into the auditorium with both the commanders and the men of prominence in the city, and Festus having commanded, Paul was brought in. <verse eid="ACT 25:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 25:24"/>And Festus says, “King Agrippa and all men being present with us, you⁺ see this one concerning whom all the multitude of the Jews pleaded with me, both in Jerusalem and here, crying out of him <char style="add">that</char> he ought not to live <char style="add">any</char> longer. <verse eid="ACT 25:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 25:25"/>But I, having understood him to have done nothing worthy of death—this one himself now having appealed to the Emperor—I determined to send <char style="add">him</char>, <verse eid="ACT 25:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 25:26"/>concerning whom I have nothing definite to write to <char style="add">my</char> lord. Therefore I have brought him before you⁺ all, and especially before you, King Agrippa, so that <char style="add">on</char> the examination having taken place, I might have something to write. <verse eid="ACT 25:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 25:27"/>For it seems absurd to me, sending a prisoner, not also to specify the charges against him.” </para>

<para style="p" vid="ACT 25:27"> BYZ and TR <char style="add">chief priest</char> BYZ and TR <char style="add">with them more than ten days</char> BYZ and TR include <char style="add">against Paul</char> F35 <char style="add">be tried by</char> RP <char style="add">he was staying</char> BYZ and TR include <char style="add">to die</char>. BYZ and TR <char style="add">no charge of the things</char> CT and F35 <char style="add">concerning these matters</char><verse eid="ACT 25:27"/></para>

<chapter eid="ACT 25"/>

<chapter number="26" style="c" sid="ACT 26"/>

<para style="s">Paul’s Testimony to Agrippa</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 26:1"/><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Acts 22:1–21</char></note><note caller="-" style="x"><char style="xt" closed="false">Acts 9:1–19</char></note>And Agrippa was saying to Paul, “It is permitted you to speak for yourself.” Then Paul, having stretched out the hand, began his defense: <verse eid="ACT 26:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 26:2"/>“Concerning all of which I am accused by the Jews, King Agrippa, I esteem myself fortunate before you, being about to defend myself today, <verse eid="ACT 26:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 26:3"/>you<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">26.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Scrivener TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">since I know you</char></note> being especially acquainted with all the customs and also controversies of the Jews. Therefore I implore <char style="add">you</char> to hear me patiently. <verse eid="ACT 26:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 26:4"/>Then indeed my manner of life, which <char style="add">is</char> from youth, having been from <char style="add">its</char> beginning among my nation and<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">26.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR do not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">and</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> in Jerusalem, all the Jews know— <verse eid="ACT 26:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 26:5"/>knowing me from the first, if they would be willing to testify—that according to the strictest sect of our religion I lived <char style="add">as</char> a Pharisee. <verse eid="ACT 26:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 26:6"/>And now I stand, being judged for the hope of the promise having been made by God to our fathers, <verse eid="ACT 26:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 26:7"/>to which our twelve tribes hope to attain, serving in earnestness night and day, the hope concerning which I am accused by the Jews, O king.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">26.7 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">O King Agrippa</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 26:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 26:8"/>Why is it judged incredible by you⁺ if God raises the dead? <verse eid="ACT 26:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 26:9"/>Therefore I indeed in myself thought <char style="add">it</char> to be necessary to do many things contrary to the name of Jesus of Nazareth, <verse eid="ACT 26:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 26:10"/>which I also did in Jerusalem. And I also locked up many of the saints in prisons, having received the authority from the chief priests; and <char style="add">on</char> their being put to death, I cast against <char style="add">them</char> a vote. <verse eid="ACT 26:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 26:11"/>And in all the synagogues, punishing them often, I was compelling <char style="add">them</char> to blaspheme. And being exceedingly furious against them, I was persecuting <char style="add">them</char> even as far as to foreign cities, <verse eid="ACT 26:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 26:12"/>during which, going to Damascus with the authority and commission of the chief priests, <verse eid="ACT 26:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 26:13"/>at midday on the road I saw, O king, a light from heaven above the brightness of the sun having shone around me and those going with me. <verse eid="ACT 26:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 26:14"/>And all of us having fallen down to the ground, I heard a voice saying to me in the Hebrew language,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">26.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">in the Aramaic language</char></note> <char style="wj">‘Saul, Saul, why do you persecute Me? It is hard for you to kick against the goads.’</char> <verse eid="ACT 26:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 26:15"/>Then I said, ‘Who are You, Lord?’ And the Lord said,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">26.15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">And He said</char></note> <char style="wj">‘I am Jesus, whom you are persecuting. </char><verse eid="ACT 26:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 26:16"/><char style="wj">But rise up and stand on your feet. For I have appeared to you for this, to appoint you as a servant and a witness both of that which you have seen of Me</char><note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">26.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR do not include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">of Me</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note><char style="wj"> and of the things in which I will appear to you, </char><verse eid="ACT 26:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 26:17"/><char style="wj">delivering you from the people and from the Gentiles, to whom I am sending you </char><verse eid="ACT 26:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 26:18"/><char style="wj">to open their eyes, so that they may turn from darkness to light and from the power of Satan to God, that they may receive forgiveness of sins and an inheritance among those having been sanctified by faith in Me.’</char> <verse eid="ACT 26:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 26:19"/>Hence, King Agrippa, I was not disobedient to the heavenly vision, <verse eid="ACT 26:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 26:20"/>but also first to those in Damascus and Jerusalem, also to all the region of Judea, and to the Gentiles, I was declaring to repent and to turn to God, doing works worthy of repentance. <verse eid="ACT 26:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 26:21"/>On account of these things the Jews, having seized me (being in the temple),<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">26.21 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the temple courts</char></note> were attempting to kill <char style="add">me</char>. <verse eid="ACT 26:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 26:22"/>Therefore, having obtained help from God up to this day, I have stood bearing witness both to small and to great, saying nothing other than that which both the prophets and Moses said was about to happen: <verse eid="ACT 26:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 26:23"/>that the Christ would suffer <char style="add">and</char>, as first through resurrection from the dead, He is about to proclaim light both to our people<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">26.23 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">light to our people</char></note> and to the Gentiles.” <verse eid="ACT 26:23"/></para>

<para style="s">Festus Interrupts Paul’s Defense</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 26:24"/>Now of him making this defense, Festus said in a loud voice, “You are insane, Paul! Much learning turns you to insanity!” <verse eid="ACT 26:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 26:25"/>But Paul says,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">26.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">But he says</char></note> “I am not insane, most excellent Festus, but I declare forth words of truth and sobriety. <verse eid="ACT 26:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 26:26"/>For the king understands concerning these things, to whom also I speak, being bold. For I am persuaded that none of these things are hidden from him, for this thing is not done in a corner. <verse eid="ACT 26:26"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 26:27"/>Do you believe the prophets, King Agrippa? I know that you believe.” <verse eid="ACT 26:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 26:28"/>Then Agrippa <char style="add">said</char> to Paul, “In so little <char style="add">time</char> do you persuade me to become a Christian?” <verse eid="ACT 26:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 26:29"/>And Paul <char style="add">said</char>, “I would wish anyhow to God, both in a little and in much, not only you, but also all those hearing me this day, to become such as I also am, except these chains.” <verse eid="ACT 26:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 26:30"/>Then<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">26.30 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">When he had spoken these things,</char></note> the king and the governor rose up, and Bernice and those sitting with them, <verse eid="ACT 26:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 26:31"/>and having withdrawn, they began speaking to one another, saying, “This man is doing nothing worthy of death or of chains.” <verse eid="ACT 26:31"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 26:32"/>Then Agrippa was saying to Festus, “This man could have been released if he had not appealed to Caesar.” <verse eid="ACT 26:32"/></para>

<chapter eid="ACT 26"/>

<chapter number="27" style="c" sid="ACT 27"/>

<para style="s">Paul Sails for Rome</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 27:1"/>Now when our sailing to Italy was determined, they delivered up both Paul and certain other prisoners to a centurion named Julius, of the cohort of Augustus.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">27.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Imperial Regiment</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 27:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 27:2"/>And having boarded a ship of Adramyttium being about to sail to the places along Asia,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">27.2 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">sail for ports along the coast of Asia</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; Asia was a Roman province in what is now western Turkey. </char></note> we set sail—Aristarchus, a Macedonian of Thessalonica, being with us. <verse eid="ACT 27:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 27:3"/>And the next day we landed at Sidon. And Julius, having treated Paul considerately, allowed <char style="add">him</char>, having gone to his<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">27.3 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Stephanus TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">some</char></note> friends, to receive care. <verse eid="ACT 27:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 27:4"/>And having set sail from there, we sailed under Cyprus because of the winds being contrary. <verse eid="ACT 27:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 27:5"/>And having sailed across the sea along Cilicia and Pamphylia, we came to Myra of Lycia. <verse eid="ACT 27:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 27:6"/>And there the centurion, having found a ship of Alexandria sailing to Italy, placed us into it. <verse eid="ACT 27:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 27:7"/>And sailing slowly for many days, and with difficulty having arrived off Cnidus, the wind not permitting us, we sailed under Crete off Salmone. <verse eid="ACT 27:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 27:8"/>And coasting along it with difficulty, we came to a certain place called Fair Havens, near to which was the city of Lasea. <verse eid="ACT 27:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 27:9"/>Now much time having passed and the voyage being already dangerous because of even the Fast<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">27.9 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> That is, Yom Kippur, the Day of Atonement</char></note> already being over, Paul was admonishing <char style="add">them</char>, <verse eid="ACT 27:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 27:10"/>saying to them, “Men, I see that the voyage is about to be with disaster and much loss, not only of the cargo and of the ship, but also of our lives.” <verse eid="ACT 27:10"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 27:11"/>But the centurion was persuaded by the pilot and the ship owner rather than by the things spoken by Paul. <verse eid="ACT 27:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 27:12"/>And the harbor being unsuitable to winter in, the majority made a decision to set sail from there, if somehow they might be able, having arrived at Phoenix—a harbor of Crete looking toward the southwest and toward the northwest—to winter <char style="add">there</char>. <verse eid="ACT 27:12"/></para>

<para style="s">The Storm at SeaJonah 1:4–10</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 27:13"/>And a south wind having blown gently, having thought to have obtained <char style="add">their</char> purpose, having weighed anchor, they began coasting along very near Crete. <verse eid="ACT 27:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 27:14"/>But not long after, there came down from it a tempestuous wind called Euroclydon.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">27.14 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Northeaster</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Euraquilo</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 27:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 27:15"/>And the ship having been caught and not being able to face the wind, having given way, we were driven along. <verse eid="ACT 27:15"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 27:16"/>And having run under a certain island called Cauda,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">27.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> NE, BYZ, and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Clauda</char></note> we were able with difficulty to gain control of the lifeboat, <verse eid="ACT 27:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 27:17"/>which having taken up, they began using supports, undergirding the ship. And fearing lest they might fall into the sandbars of Syrtis, having lowered the gear,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">27.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the sails</char></note> thus they were driven along. <verse eid="ACT 27:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 27:18"/>And <char style="add">in</char> our being storm-tossed violently, on the next day they began to make a jettison of cargo, <verse eid="ACT 27:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 27:19"/>and on the third <char style="add">day</char> they cast away the tackle of the ship with <char style="add">their</char> own hands.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">27.19 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">we cast away the tackle of the ship with our own hands</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 27:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 27:20"/>And neither sun nor stars appearing for many days, and no small storm lying on <char style="add">us</char>, from then on all hope of our being saved was abandoned. <verse eid="ACT 27:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 27:21"/>There being also much time without food, at that time having stood up in their midst, Paul said, “It was necessary indeed, O men, having been obedient to me, not to have set sail from Crete and to have incurred this disaster and loss. <verse eid="ACT 27:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 27:22"/>And now I exhort you⁺ to take heart, for there will be no loss of life from among you⁺—only of the ship. <verse eid="ACT 27:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 27:23"/>For this night an angel of God, whose I am and whom I serve, stood by me, <verse eid="ACT 27:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 27:24"/>saying, ‘Do not be afraid, Paul. It is necessary for you to stand before Caesar. And behold, God has granted to you all those sailing with you.’ <verse eid="ACT 27:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 27:25"/>Therefore take heart, men, for I believe God that it will be thus, according to the way it has been said to me. <verse eid="ACT 27:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 27:26"/>But it is necessary for us to fall upon a certain island.” <verse eid="ACT 27:26"/></para>

<para style="s">The Shipwreck</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 27:27"/>And when the fourteenth night had come of us being driven about in the Adriatic,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">27.27 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> The Adriatic Sea referred to an area extending well south of Italy to include the central portion of the Mediterranean Sea.</char></note> toward the middle of the night the sailors began sensing some land to be drawing near to them. <verse eid="ACT 27:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 27:28"/>And having taken soundings, they found twenty fathoms.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">27.28 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">20 fathoms</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 120 feet or 36.6 meters.</char></note> And having gone a little farther and having taken soundings again, they found fifteen fathoms.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">27.28 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> </char><char style="fq" closed="false">15 fathoms</char><char style="ft" closed="false"> is approximately 90 feet or 27.4 meters.</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 27:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="ACT 27:29"/>And fearing, lest we might fall<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">27.29 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Stephanus TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">they would run aground</char></note> somewhere on rocky places, having cast four anchors out of the stern, they were praying for day to come. <verse eid="ACT 27:29"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 27:30"/>And the sailors seeking to flee out of the ship and having let down the lifeboat into the sea under pretense as being about to cast out anchors from the bow, <verse eid="ACT 27:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 27:31"/>Paul said to the centurion and to the soldiers, “Unless these remain in the ship, you⁺ are not able to be saved.” <verse eid="ACT 27:31"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="ACT 27:32"/>Then the soldiers cut away the ropes of the lifeboat and allowed it to fall away. <verse eid="ACT 27:32"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="ACT 27:33"/>And until that day was about to come, Paul kept urging all to partake of food, saying, “Today <char style="add">is</char> the fourteenth day you⁺ continue waiting without eating, having taken nothing. <verse eid="ACT 27:33"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="ACT 27:34"/>Therefore I exhort you⁺ to take food, for this is for your⁺<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">27.34 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> F35 </char><char style="fq" closed="false">our</char></note> preservation; for not one hair of your⁺ head will perish.” <verse eid="ACT 27:34"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="ACT 27:35"/>And having said these things and having taken bread, he gave thanks to God before all; and having broken <char style="add">it</char>, he began to eat. <verse eid="ACT 27:35"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="ACT 27:36"/>And all, having been encouraged, also took food themselves. <verse eid="ACT 27:36"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="ACT 27:37"/>And we were altogether two hundred seventy-six<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">27.37 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> WH </char><char style="fq" closed="false">seventy-six</char></note> souls in the ship. <verse eid="ACT 27:37"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="ACT 27:38"/>And having been filled with food, they began to lighten the ship, casting out the wheat into the sea. <verse eid="ACT 27:38"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="ACT 27:39"/>And when it was day, they did not recognize the land, but they noticed a certain bay, having a shore on which they decided to drive the ship if they could.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">27.39 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ </char><char style="fq" closed="false">if possible</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 27:39"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="ACT 27:40"/>And having cut away the anchors, they left <char style="add">them</char> in the sea, at the same time having loosened the ropes of the rudders. And having hoisted the foresail to the blowing <char style="add">wind</char>, they began making for the shore. <verse eid="ACT 27:40"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="ACT 27:41"/>But having fallen into a place between two seas, they ran the vessel aground. And indeed the bow, having stuck fast, remained immovable, and the stern was being broken up by the violence of the waves. <verse eid="ACT 27:41"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="ACT 27:42"/>Now the plan of the soldiers was that they should kill the prisoners, lest anyone, having swum away, should escape. <verse eid="ACT 27:42"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="ACT 27:43"/>But the centurion, desiring to save Paul, hindered them of the plan; and he commanded those being able to swim, having cast <char style="add">themselves</char> off first, to go out on the land, <verse eid="ACT 27:43"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="44" style="v" sid="ACT 27:44"/>and the rest, some indeed on boards and some on things from the ship. And thus it came to pass <char style="add">that</char> all were brought safely to the land. <verse eid="ACT 27:44"/></para>

<chapter eid="ACT 27"/>

<chapter number="28" style="c" sid="ACT 28"/>

<para style="s">Ashore on Malta</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="ACT 28:1"/>And having been saved, then we found out that the island is called Malta.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">28.1 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> WH </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Melitene</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 28:1"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="ACT 28:2"/>And the natives were showing not <char style="add">just</char> the ordinary kindness to us. For having kindled a fire, they received all of us because of the rain setting in and because of the cold. <verse eid="ACT 28:2"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="ACT 28:3"/>Now <char style="add">on</char> Paul having gathered a multitude of sticks and having laid <char style="add">them</char> on the fire, a viper, having come out from the heat, fastened <char style="add">itself</char> on his hand. <verse eid="ACT 28:3"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="ACT 28:4"/>And when the natives saw the beast hanging from his hand, they began to say to one another, “By all means this man is a murderer whom, having been saved from the sea, Dike<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">28.4 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Justice</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; the Greek goddess of justice is </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Dike</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> did not permit to live.” <verse eid="ACT 28:4"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="ACT 28:5"/>Then indeed, having shaken off the creature into the fire, he suffered no harm. <verse eid="ACT 28:5"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="ACT 28:6"/>But they were expecting him to be about to become inflamed or suddenly to fall down dead. But <char style="add">on</char> their waiting a great while and seeing nothing amiss happening to him, having changed their opinion, they began declaring him to be a god. <verse eid="ACT 28:6"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="ACT 28:7"/>Now in the <char style="add">parts</char> around that place were lands of the chief of the island, named Publius, who, having received us, entertained <char style="add">us</char> hospitably <char style="add">for</char> three days. <verse eid="ACT 28:7"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="ACT 28:8"/>And it came to pass <char style="add">that</char> the father of Publius was lying, oppressed with fevers and dysentery, toward whom Paul, having entered and having prayed, having laid the hands on him, healed him. <verse eid="ACT 28:8"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="ACT 28:9"/>And <char style="add">on</char> this having taken place, also the rest in the island having infirmities were coming and were healed, <verse eid="ACT 28:9"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="ACT 28:10"/>who also honored us with many honors, and on setting sail, they laid on <char style="add">us</char> the things for <char style="add">our</char> needs. <verse eid="ACT 28:10"/></para>

<para style="s">Paul Arrives in Italy</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="ACT 28:11"/>And after three months, we sailed in an Alexandrian ship having wintered in the island, with a figurehead of the Dioscuri.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">28.11 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Or </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the Twin Brothers</char><char style="ft" closed="false">; that is, the Greek gods Castor and Pollux</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 28:11"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="ACT 28:12"/>And having put in at Syracuse, we stayed three days, <verse eid="ACT 28:12"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="ACT 28:13"/>from where, having cast off,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">28.13 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">having sailed around</char></note> we arrived at Rhegium. And after one day, a south wind having come up, on the second day we came to Puteoli, <verse eid="ACT 28:13"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="ACT 28:14"/>where having found <char style="add">some</char> brothers, we were entreated to remain with them seven days. And so we came to Rome. <verse eid="ACT 28:14"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="ACT 28:15"/>And the brothers from there, having heard the things concerning us, came out as far as the Forum of Appius<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">28.15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> The Forum of Appius was about 43 miles or 70 kilometers from Rome.</char></note> and the Three Taverns<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">28.15 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> The Three Taverns was about 35 miles or 57 kilometers from Rome.</char></note> to meet us, whom Paul having seen, having given thanks to God, took courage. <verse eid="ACT 28:15"/></para>

<para style="s">Paul Preaches at RomeIsaiah 6:1–13</para>

<para style="p"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="ACT 28:16"/>Now when we came to Rome,<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">28.16 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">the centurion delivered up the prisoners to the captain of the barrack, but</char><char style="ft" closed="false">.</char></note> Paul was allowed to stay by himself with the soldier guarding him. <verse eid="ACT 28:16"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="ACT 28:17"/>And it came to pass after three days <char style="add">that</char> he<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">28.17 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">Paul</char></note> called together those being leaders of the Jews. And <char style="add">on</char> their having come together, he was saying to them, “Men, brothers, having done nothing against the people or the customs of our fathers, I was delivered from Jerusalem <char style="add">as</char> a prisoner into the hands of the Romans, <verse eid="ACT 28:17"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="ACT 28:18"/>who, having examined me, were wanting to let <char style="add">me</char> go on account of not one cause of death existing in me. <verse eid="ACT 28:18"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="ACT 28:19"/>But <char style="add">on</char> the Jews objecting, I was compelled to appeal to Caesar, not as having anything to accuse my nation. <verse eid="ACT 28:19"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="ACT 28:20"/>For this cause, therefore, I have called to see you⁺ and to speak to <char style="add">you</char>. For because of the hope of Israel, I have around <char style="add">me</char> this chain.” <verse eid="ACT 28:20"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="ACT 28:21"/>And they said to him, “We received neither letters concerning you from Judea, nor did any of the brothers having arrived report or say anything evil concerning you. <verse eid="ACT 28:21"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="ACT 28:22"/>But we count it worthy to hear from you what you think, for truly, concerning this sect, it is known to us that it is spoken against everywhere.” <verse eid="ACT 28:22"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="ACT 28:23"/>Then, having appointed to him a day, many came to him to the lodging, to whom he expounded from morning to evening, fully testifying to the kingdom of God and persuading them concerning Jesus from both the Law of Moses and the Prophets. <verse eid="ACT 28:23"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="ACT 28:24"/>And indeed, some were persuaded of the things being said, but some refused to believe. <verse eid="ACT 28:24"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="ACT 28:25"/>And being discordant with one another they began to leave, Paul having said one word: “The Holy Spirit spoke rightly by the prophet Isaiah to your⁺<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">28.25 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR </char><char style="fq" closed="false">our</char></note> fathers, <verse eid="ACT 28:25"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="ACT 28:26"/>saying: </para>

<para style="q1" vid="ACT 28:26">‘Go to this people and say, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 28:26">“In hearing you⁺ will hear and never understand; </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 28:26">and in seeing you⁺ will see and never perceive.” <verse eid="ACT 28:26"/></para>

<para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="ACT 28:27"/>For the heart of this people grew dull, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 28:27">and with the ears they barely hear, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 28:27">and they have closed their eyes, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="ACT 28:27">lest ever they should see with the eyes, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 28:27">and should hear with the ears, </para>

<para style="q2" vid="ACT 28:27">and should understand with the heart, </para>

<para style="q1" vid="ACT 28:27">and should turn, and I will heal them.’ <note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">28.27 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> Isaiah 6:9–10 (see also LXX)</char></note><verse eid="ACT 28:27"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="ACT 28:28"/>Therefore be it known to you⁺ that this salvation of God has been sent to the Gentiles, and they will listen!”<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">28.28 </char><char style="ft" closed="false"> BYZ and TR include </char><char style="fq" closed="false">29</char><char style="fq" closed="false">And on his having said this, the Jews went away, having much dispute among themselves.</char></note> <verse eid="ACT 28:28"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="ACT 28:30"/>And he stayed two whole years in his own rented house, and he was welcoming all those coming to him, <verse eid="ACT 28:30"/></para>

<para style="p"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="ACT 28:31"/>proclaiming the kingdom of God and teaching the things concerning the Lord Jesus Christ with all boldness, freely. <verse eid="ACT 28:31"/></para>

<chapter eid="ACT 28"/>

</usx>
